WEBVTT

1
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.042
While people in other parts
of the world fought for their survival,

2
00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:07.292
in India,
a mighty civilization was being forged.

3
00:01:08.792 --> 00:01:12.125
A place where people
of all faiths lived like one family.

4
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:16.208
But this temple soon fell victim
to aggressive invasions.

5
00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:21.333
In the 16th century,
after winning the battle of Panipat,

6
00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:24.708
the Mughal Empire's flag soared
high over the throne of Delhi.

7
00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:30.292
In those dark times, countless rulers
and kingdoms fought for survival.

8
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.583
For the next century, no one in India

9
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.708
could bring down the might
of the Mughal Empire.

10
00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:39.125
In the 17th century,

11
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:42.750
the most powerful, ruthless,
and merciless Mughal Emperor,

12
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:44.917
Aurangzeb, sat on the throne,

13
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.542
imposing unimaginable tyranny.

14
00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.375
But whenever terror
and cruelty rise on earth,

15
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:59.458
a great soul is born to protect it.

16
00:02:00.292 --> 00:02:01.452
And that fated moment dawned,

17
00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:04.750
when the very essence
of Goddess Bhavani and Lord Shiva

18
00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:06.309
was born from the womb of Mother Jijau,

19
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:09.292
within the family of Shahajiraje Bhonsle.

20
00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:12.292
Har Har Mahadev!

21
00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:14.695
The one to protect this land
from the atrocities of Aurang,

22
00:02:14.958 --> 00:02:17.167
the one who ignited the flame of Swarajya

23
00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:19.167
and founded the Maratha Empire,

24
00:02:21.042 --> 00:02:23.125
was none other than
the great hero of this land…

25
00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:25.875
Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj!

26
00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:32.667
His fight was never against any religion.

27
00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:36.583
His struggle
was against oppression and tyranny.

28
00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.833
Fearing his growing power,

29
00:02:40.208 --> 00:02:42.750
Aurang launched numerous
attacks on Swarajya,

30
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.750
but every time, he was defeated.

31
00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.208
Swarajya!

32
00:02:46.292 --> 00:02:50.792
If anyone on this earth could challenge
Aurangzeb and his merciless empire,

33
00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:53.667
it was the lion of the Deccan,

34
00:02:54.042 --> 00:02:55.292
the brave, the valiant…

35
00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:57.708
Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj!

36
00:02:57.792 --> 00:02:59.750
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

37
00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:14.167
RED FORT

38
00:03:15.417 --> 00:03:19.208
From Bengal,
Shaista Khan sends a royal gift, my Lord.

39
00:03:22.292 --> 00:03:24.125
In the war in Tibet, the Mughals

40
00:03:24.708 --> 00:03:26.375
have emerged victorious, Your Majesty.

41
00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:27.833
- Wonderful!
- Amazing!

42
00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:29.458
- Superb!
- Wonderful!

43
00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.625
- Amazing!
- Superb!

44
00:03:35.125 --> 00:03:37.167
May the Lord's greatness
continue to ascend!

45
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:43.653
We have received urgent news
from the Deccan, Your Majesty.

46
00:03:44.792 --> 00:03:46.125
The Shiva of the Deccan,

47
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:48.125
the Chhatrapati of the Marathas,

48
00:03:49.083 --> 00:03:50.875
has passed on to the afterlife!

49
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.500
- Glory be to Allah!
- Glory be to Allah!

50
00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:57.292
- Glory be to Allah!
- Glory be to Allah!

51
00:03:58.542 --> 00:03:59.625
Upon hearing this,

52
00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:04.833
I can already imagine the Mughal flag

53
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:07.708
soaring over Hindustan!

54
00:04:07.792 --> 00:04:09.875
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

55
00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:11.083
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

56
00:04:11.542 --> 00:04:12.542
With Shivaji's demise,

57
00:04:13.792 --> 00:04:16.833
the Deccan will inevitably fall
under our empire's control!

58
00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:18.458
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

59
00:04:18.542 --> 00:04:19.708
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

60
00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.708
While imprisoned in Agra,

61
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:24.167
he managed to escape

62
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.042
both death and Your Majesty's grasp.

63
00:04:27.792 --> 00:04:29.125
Since then,

64
00:04:30.292 --> 00:04:32.208
we have failed to conquer the Deccan.

65
00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:33.417
At last,

66
00:04:34.125 --> 00:04:37.833
Your Majesty's only unfulfilled
dream has been realized today.

67
00:04:38.292 --> 00:04:40.625
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

68
00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:41.829
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

69
00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:45.708
My eager ears still long for good news,
yet none comes, even today.

70
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:54.042
A foe like Siva…

71
00:04:57.083 --> 00:04:58.667
Comes once in a lifetime.

72
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.167
Oh, Allah, this grievance with You
shall linger in my heart forever!

73
00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:12.708
Keep the gates of heaven wide open…

74
00:05:15.792 --> 00:05:16.833
The lion is coming!

75
00:05:23.042 --> 00:05:24.167
Celebrate!

76
00:05:28.917 --> 00:05:30.458
Make the poor people rich!

77
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.917
Celebrate the fall of the Maratha Empire!

78
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.625
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

79
00:05:41.875 --> 00:05:45.917
BURHANPUR
JANUARY 1681

80
00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:40.708
Sire Khan Zamaan,

81
00:06:42.542 --> 00:06:44.625
the taxes collected from the non-Muslims

82
00:06:44.833 --> 00:06:47.000
are quickly filling the treasury!

83
00:06:47.292 --> 00:06:48.208
- Wow!
- That's amazing!

84
00:06:48.292 --> 00:06:50.875
Since Shivaji's death, people,
gripped by fear for their lives,

85
00:06:53.208 --> 00:06:55.333
are willingly offering us their wealth!

86
00:06:55.417 --> 00:06:56.250
Glory be to Allah!

87
00:06:56.333 --> 00:06:57.583
Glory be to Allah!

88
00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:58.708
Glory be to Allah!

89
00:06:59.417 --> 00:07:01.750
That's why I'm getting a massage, Kakkad!

90
00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.542
My bones are stiff
from a lack of movement!

91
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.000
Unfortunately,

92
00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:07.792
there's been no battle

93
00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:09.500
or pillaging lately.

94
00:07:09.833 --> 00:07:12.500
May God keep your strong body fit
and healthy, Sire!

95
00:07:13.458 --> 00:07:15.375
Burhanpur is like a gold mine, Sire!

96
00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:18.000
It is the lifeline of the Mughal Empire.

97
00:07:19.208 --> 00:07:22.458
You never know when you might have
to defend it from someone's prying eyes!

98
00:07:22.958 --> 00:07:24.542
Who would dare attack us?

99
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.583
The Rajputs are busy guarding
their own empire!

100
00:07:30.167 --> 00:07:32.087
And the Marathas
have been left without a leader.

101
00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:35.375
My advice is to sip some
kahwah and stay alert.

102
00:07:36.208 --> 00:07:38.417
For death's summons

103
00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:41.250
and uninvited guests…

104
00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.667
Always arrive without a warning!

105
00:07:54.875 --> 00:07:56.000
Sire!

106
00:07:56.083 --> 00:07:57.000
Mar… Mar…

107
00:07:57.083 --> 00:07:58.417
What are you saying?

108
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.458
The Maratha army is fast approaching!

109
00:08:05.167 --> 00:08:07.750
Close the gates!

110
00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:09.667
Be on guard!

111
00:08:10.375 --> 00:08:12.667
The Marathas are here!

112
00:08:33.583 --> 00:08:35.125
Charge!

113
00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.958
Charge!

114
00:08:47.208 --> 00:08:48.208
Let them come!

115
00:08:48.792 --> 00:08:51.000
We will turn the Burhanpur border
into their tomb!

116
00:08:51.458 --> 00:08:52.458
Indeed, Sire!

117
00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.830
Not a single Maratha
will be able to set foot inside!

118
00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:02.375
Sire!

119
00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.625
The Maratha army has breached Burhanpur!

120
00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:43.625
Har Har Mahadev!

121
00:11:30.917 --> 00:11:34.833
Har Har Mahadev!

122
00:11:37.292 --> 00:11:38.292
What are you waiting for?

123
00:11:43.083 --> 00:11:45.458
Har Har Mahadev!

124
00:12:00.417 --> 00:12:03.458
Har Har Mahadev!

125
00:12:19.417 --> 00:12:20.833
Goddess Jagdamba!

126
00:13:26.458 --> 00:13:28.042
Mother!

127
00:13:29.042 --> 00:13:30.667
Mother!

128
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.708
My son!

129
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.250
Someone save him!

130
00:13:48.333 --> 00:13:49.333
My son!

131
00:14:11.583 --> 00:14:13.083
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

132
00:16:25.333 --> 00:16:26.833
Raje!

133
00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:29.625
Shields!

134
00:19:50.958 --> 00:19:52.042
Khan Zamaan,

135
00:19:52.792 --> 00:19:54.333
tell your master…

136
00:19:55.125 --> 00:19:56.500
The lion may have fallen,

137
00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:00.000
but his chhaava
still prowls these forests!

138
00:20:01.042 --> 00:20:05.625
We will tear the Mughal Empire apart
if it dares challenge the Marathas!

139
00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:08.292
We make no noise!

140
00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.750
We swiftly hunt our prey down!

141
00:20:17.542 --> 00:20:22.375
- Hail Goddess…
- Bhavani!

142
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.875
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

143
00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:28.917
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

144
00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:32.667
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

145
00:20:59.375 --> 00:21:00.958
Fasten it well, Dhanaji!

146
00:21:01.583 --> 00:21:02.667
It's bleeding heavily!

147
00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.250
Uncle Yesaji, let it bleed a bit.

148
00:21:06.125 --> 00:21:08.846
Every drop of blood spilled
for Swarajya sanctifies this Mughal land!

149
00:21:10.708 --> 00:21:11.542
Well said!

150
00:21:11.625 --> 00:21:14.667
Secure, seal, and send the treasure
to Raigad, Santa.

151
00:21:15.833 --> 00:21:16.667
Understood, Father.

152
00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.667
But hauling all the treasure
will be a challenge.

153
00:21:20.708 --> 00:21:22.018
The hunger isn't for the treasure,

154
00:21:22.042 --> 00:21:24.042
but for defeating the enemy, Santa.

155
00:21:24.958 --> 00:21:28.125
Aurangzeb should only see
the ruins of Burhanpur!

156
00:21:29.875 --> 00:21:30.875
As you wish!

157
00:21:36.583 --> 00:21:38.292
- Anta?
- Yes?

158
00:21:38.625 --> 00:21:39.625
What's happening?

159
00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.042
Why is our Crown Prince's favorite

160
00:21:43.458 --> 00:21:45.708
Kavi Kalash dining alone here?

161
00:21:47.125 --> 00:21:49.042
A poet's heart is a friend to all

162
00:21:49.292 --> 00:21:51.167
He embraces blooms, birds
And nature's call

163
00:21:51.417 --> 00:21:53.083
He welcomes all with love to share

164
00:21:53.792 --> 00:21:55.833
He's not the selfish kind

165
00:21:55.917 --> 00:21:57.583
Who just decorates the air

166
00:21:57.667 --> 00:21:58.667
Amazing!

167
00:21:58.833 --> 00:22:02.000
How can anyone leave such
a person alone?

168
00:22:02.583 --> 00:22:04.875
I'm a man from the Mughal lands

169
00:22:05.375 --> 00:22:07.292
living among the Marathas.

170
00:22:07.875 --> 00:22:09.208
Tell me, Antaji,

171
00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:12.875
why would anyone want to share
a meal with me?

172
00:22:14.125 --> 00:22:15.125
You have a point.

173
00:22:16.208 --> 00:22:18.792
Does this not make you sad?

174
00:22:21.583 --> 00:22:23.208
If the Lord is pleased

175
00:22:23.458 --> 00:22:24.875
There is neither shame nor fear

176
00:22:25.458 --> 00:22:29.000
After all, this Kavi Kalash's friend
Is Sambhaji Shivraj!

177
00:22:29.167 --> 00:22:30.167
Well said!

178
00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.500
Aaisahib!

179
00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:37.958
Aaisahib!

180
00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:40.542
Aaisahib!

181
00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:42.750
Yes, Shambhu?

182
00:22:44.625 --> 00:22:45.625
Abasahib!

183
00:22:46.375 --> 00:22:48.833
When will this smoke clear, Abasahib?

184
00:22:49.833 --> 00:22:52.167
As long as the flame
of Swarajya burns bright,

185
00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:54.333
this smoke shall rise, Shambhu!

186
00:23:09.083 --> 00:23:10.083
Crown Prince.

187
00:23:16.875 --> 00:23:19.167
Uncle Hambir, please call me Shambhu.

188
00:23:21.417 --> 00:23:23.333
My ears yearn to hear "Shambhu."

189
00:23:30.333 --> 00:23:32.875
I see your father's image in you,

190
00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:39.042
perhaps, that's why I hesitate.

191
00:23:41.708 --> 00:23:45.833
And I get the strength of Abasahib
and Aaisahib's blessings from you!

192
00:23:47.458 --> 00:23:49.083
Even when I face a thousand enemies,

193
00:23:49.167 --> 00:23:51.708
I know your eyes
are always watching over me!

194
00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:54.500
I am…

195
00:23:55.458 --> 00:23:57.299
Not as great as
you make me out to be, Shambhu.

196
00:23:59.708 --> 00:24:04.042
All I know is that every drop
in these veins…

197
00:24:06.375 --> 00:24:07.736
Is ready to be sacrificed for you!

198
00:24:09.625 --> 00:24:10.625
Uncle!

199
00:24:14.917 --> 00:24:15.917
Let's go.

200
00:24:17.958 --> 00:24:19.292
Everyone is waiting for you.

201
00:24:37.625 --> 00:24:39.083
This is not just a victory,

202
00:24:40.417 --> 00:24:41.417
it is a roar…

203
00:24:42.708 --> 00:24:45.708
That will reach Aurang's ears
and proclaim that

204
00:24:45.792 --> 00:24:48.708
Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj
is still alive!

205
00:24:51.500 --> 00:24:52.768
This is not the end of the Marathas,

206
00:24:52.792 --> 00:24:54.542
but the beginning
of the Mughals' downfall.

207
00:24:55.125 --> 00:24:57.875
We will march forward in this battle,
honoring all religions,

208
00:24:57.958 --> 00:25:00.458
for this war is not against
a particular sect.

209
00:25:01.958 --> 00:25:04.583
This war is to establish Swarajya,

210
00:25:06.042 --> 00:25:08.667
a land where people
of all faiths can live in peace.

211
00:25:10.667 --> 00:25:13.958
A nation where everyone can walk
with their heads held high, like kings.

212
00:25:16.750 --> 00:25:19.333
And if Aurang or devils like him…

213
00:25:20.125 --> 00:25:23.750
Dare to challenge
Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj's Swarajya,

214
00:25:23.875 --> 00:25:25.667
then I swear by Goddess Jagdamba,

215
00:25:25.833 --> 00:25:28.750
we shall erupt like a volcano
and turn them to dust!

216
00:25:30.792 --> 00:25:32.792
We will crush every challenge,

217
00:25:33.667 --> 00:25:35.250
shatter every conspiracy,

218
00:25:35.583 --> 00:25:38.750
and we will not stop until
Abasahib's vision is fulfilled!

219
00:25:38.833 --> 00:25:40.125
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

220
00:25:40.208 --> 00:25:41.625
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

221
00:25:41.708 --> 00:25:42.792
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

222
00:25:42.875 --> 00:25:44.083
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

223
00:25:44.167 --> 00:25:45.500
Har Har Mahadev!

224
00:25:45.583 --> 00:25:47.917
Har Har Mahadev!

225
00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:50.292
RAIGAD

226
00:25:50.583 --> 00:25:54.292
The royal throne is being prepared
for the other Chhatrapati, Annaji.

227
00:25:54.625 --> 00:25:58.792
I heard that the Crown Prince
left Burhanpur in ruins!

228
00:25:59.125 --> 00:26:01.875
He turned their celebrations
into mourning!

229
00:26:03.000 --> 00:26:05.792
Shambhu has shattered our dreams as well.

230
00:26:07.292 --> 00:26:12.000
He pardoned our past misdemeanors
and gave us a second chance,

231
00:26:12.083 --> 00:26:13.250
but for what?

232
00:26:14.625 --> 00:26:16.708
To suffocate in silence or

233
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:18.792
to live a life of restraint?

234
00:26:20.375 --> 00:26:22.583
This new life will be in vain

235
00:26:22.667 --> 00:26:26.333
if I cannot see Ramraje crowned
as Chhatrapati!

236
00:26:28.917 --> 00:26:31.292
The reign will be ours.

237
00:26:33.167 --> 00:26:35.750
But this Sambha…

238
00:26:37.833 --> 00:26:39.833
Once he ascends the throne,

239
00:26:39.917 --> 00:26:43.167
our existence or demise
will no longer matter!

240
00:26:45.667 --> 00:26:46.667
Since childhood,

241
00:26:46.750 --> 00:26:50.167
Sambhaji has been like a thorn
in my side,

242
00:26:50.250 --> 00:26:52.083
constantly tormenting me.

243
00:26:59.708 --> 00:27:00.958
He was of the same age when…

244
00:27:03.833 --> 00:27:07.000
After escaping Aurangzeb's
imprisonment in Agra,

245
00:27:08.167 --> 00:27:09.607
His Late Majesty
and the Crown Prince

246
00:27:09.667 --> 00:27:11.167
were wandering from place to place.

247
00:27:12.875 --> 00:27:15.250
Every Mughal soldier was ordered

248
00:27:15.917 --> 00:27:22.167
to arrest any father-son pair in disguise!

249
00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:28.083
They parted ways

250
00:27:28.958 --> 00:27:31.042
to protect each other's life.

251
00:27:34.083 --> 00:27:38.000
To save the Crown Prince
from being captured,

252
00:27:40.208 --> 00:27:43.458
His Majesty even staged his own funeral.

253
00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:50.833
To deceive the Mughals,

254
00:27:52.667 --> 00:27:55.208
the entire Deccan mourned.

255
00:28:01.125 --> 00:28:02.708
So, how can one who is destined…

256
00:28:03.750 --> 00:28:04.750
To hide,

257
00:28:05.500 --> 00:28:06.500
to run,

258
00:28:09.042 --> 00:28:10.417
and die…

259
00:28:13.625 --> 00:28:15.583
Ever claim the throne?

260
00:28:20.667 --> 00:28:22.750
No matter who is crowned,

261
00:28:25.583 --> 00:28:28.833
my son, Ramraje, is the true king!

262
00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:48.667
You know it, and I know too

263
00:28:48.917 --> 00:28:53.917
You were my world
And it still holds true

264
00:28:54.375 --> 00:28:59.458
I want to dwell

265
00:28:59.792 --> 00:29:05.083
Dwell in every breath you take

266
00:29:05.458 --> 00:29:09.792
You are my beloved

267
00:29:10.875 --> 00:29:15.375
You are my beloved

268
00:29:16.125 --> 00:29:21.125
You know it, and I know too

269
00:29:21.750 --> 00:29:26.708
You were my world
And it still holds true

270
00:29:27.167 --> 00:29:32.417
These breaths
What meaning do they bear?

271
00:29:32.667 --> 00:29:37.917
They come and go, with no care

272
00:29:38.167 --> 00:29:42.583
You are my world

273
00:29:42.750 --> 00:29:43.583
Maharani?

274
00:29:43.667 --> 00:29:48.000
You were, and always will be, eternally

275
00:29:49.125 --> 00:29:51.750
You know it

276
00:29:51.833 --> 00:29:53.875
- What happened here?
- And I know too

277
00:29:55.708 --> 00:29:58.167
It seems we must ward off
the evil once again!

278
00:29:58.792 --> 00:30:01.375
Dharauma has raised me to be a man

279
00:30:01.958 --> 00:30:05.333
who cannot be harmed
by any sword or spear!

280
00:30:07.292 --> 00:30:09.792
Mother, how can anyone cast
an evil eye on the one

281
00:30:10.667 --> 00:30:12.542
upon whom
the entire Swarajya's hopes rest?

282
00:30:23.167 --> 00:30:24.167
Shri-Sakhi!

283
00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:27.542
Can I ask you something?

284
00:30:28.417 --> 00:30:31.125
Usually, when kings and emperors
return from battle,

285
00:30:31.583 --> 00:30:35.708
their queens pretend to be angry,
to show their love and concern!

286
00:30:37.042 --> 00:30:39.583
But look at me, I can't stop smiling!

287
00:30:41.292 --> 00:30:43.000
Would it be fair to push someone,

288
00:30:43.292 --> 00:30:47.208
who just returned from battle,
into another fight?

289
00:30:50.167 --> 00:30:53.417
How do you always answer
before I even ask?

290
00:30:54.583 --> 00:30:57.917
Because I am not just your wife,
but your Shri-Sakhi!

291
00:30:59.875 --> 00:31:01.917
And as for this smile,

292
00:31:02.417 --> 00:31:04.625
rumors say that not just in the Deccan,

293
00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:08.750
but if any woman in the North
hears Sambhaji Bhonsle's name,

294
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.750
she can't help but smile!

295
00:31:14.958 --> 00:31:17.333
You know more about me

296
00:31:18.125 --> 00:31:20.833
than I know about myself.

297
00:31:21.125 --> 00:31:23.167
These are just hearsay.

298
00:31:23.875 --> 00:31:26.125
It is easy to keep track of them.

299
00:31:28.125 --> 00:31:32.083
I even know what hides in your heart!

300
00:31:34.417 --> 00:31:35.417
I see!

301
00:31:37.250 --> 00:31:38.292
Then tell me,

302
00:31:39.458 --> 00:31:42.792
what am I thinking about right now?

303
00:31:43.750 --> 00:31:47.000
Right now, there's only one thing
troubling you.

304
00:31:47.917 --> 00:31:49.833
But don't worry,

305
00:31:50.667 --> 00:31:53.458
I've already made your dream come true!

306
00:31:59.042 --> 00:32:00.042
What?

307
00:32:09.667 --> 00:32:13.375
This kingdom is nothing
but the will of the divine, Shambhu!

308
00:32:54.333 --> 00:32:56.792
The one whose blessings
you've longed for…

309
00:32:57.750 --> 00:33:01.333
Has been here all along,
waiting to bless you!

310
00:33:05.083 --> 00:33:09.292
He's seeing his dreams
being fulfilled through your eyes!

311
00:33:20.375 --> 00:33:24.542
Sometimes, I feel you care more
for Hindavi Swarajya than I do!

312
00:33:25.583 --> 00:33:28.167
I think the way you think!

313
00:33:30.083 --> 00:33:32.125
Because this Sakhi
doesn't live in this palace…

314
00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:35.833
But in her Shri's heart!

315
00:33:45.125 --> 00:33:48.667
In a place where the Lord
once controlled everything,

316
00:33:50.042 --> 00:33:51.583
now faces a different fate.

317
00:33:53.583 --> 00:33:56.458
The Marathas left only dust in their wake!

318
00:33:58.042 --> 00:33:59.042
The Marathas?

319
00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:03.000
Their claws have been permanently clipped!

320
00:34:04.083 --> 00:34:05.083
How could they attack?

321
00:34:06.125 --> 00:34:07.485
Especially a place like Burhanpur!

322
00:34:09.625 --> 00:34:10.625
Was Khan Zamaan

323
00:34:11.417 --> 00:34:13.625
even in his right mind
when he wrote this letter?

324
00:34:14.792 --> 00:34:17.750
Another storm has risen
from the Deccan, my Lord!

325
00:34:18.750 --> 00:34:19.750
And its name is…

326
00:34:21.167 --> 00:34:22.625
Sambhaji Bhonsle.

327
00:34:45.875 --> 00:34:47.500
Why is Siva not here, Ramsingh?

328
00:34:48.542 --> 00:34:51.417
It's Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj.

329
00:35:00.375 --> 00:35:02.833
Maharaj is not well, my Lord.

330
00:35:03.208 --> 00:35:04.667
He is down with a high fever.

331
00:35:19.333 --> 00:35:21.292
Do you never get a fever, Crown Prince?

332
00:35:21.458 --> 00:35:25.875
I don't, but many others
catch a fever because of me!

333
00:35:34.583 --> 00:35:36.208
Siva is gone,

334
00:35:38.583 --> 00:35:40.833
but he left behind his vision.

335
00:35:47.125 --> 00:35:49.500
Oh, God, don't let me fall
into despair again!

336
00:35:52.667 --> 00:35:56.625
Protect Sambha's life
until I reach the Deccan!

337
00:35:58.208 --> 00:36:00.375
O Lord of Lords

338
00:36:00.458 --> 00:36:02.542
O Essence of all

339
00:36:02.625 --> 00:36:04.792
O Mighty One

340
00:36:04.875 --> 00:36:06.958
O Commander of Armies

341
00:36:07.042 --> 00:36:09.125
O Invincible Lord

342
00:36:09.208 --> 00:36:11.292
O Beloved One

343
00:36:11.375 --> 00:36:13.500
O Supreme Man

344
00:36:13.583 --> 00:36:15.667
O Ultimate Being

345
00:36:15.750 --> 00:36:17.833
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

346
00:36:17.917 --> 00:36:20.500
With storms that surge in veins untold!

347
00:36:24.167 --> 00:36:26.625
The era stirs with a thunderous cry

348
00:36:26.708 --> 00:36:29.333
The storm rises, shaking earth and sky!

349
00:36:30.708 --> 00:36:34.833
In saffron's glory the sky ignites

350
00:36:35.333 --> 00:36:38.000
The storm is here blazing bright!

351
00:36:39.667 --> 00:36:43.833
One eye holds tears, the other, desire

352
00:36:44.083 --> 00:36:46.667
The storm has come raging like fire!

353
00:36:48.458 --> 00:36:49.958
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

354
00:36:50.042 --> 00:36:52.976
- Congratulations, Sambhaji Maharaj!
- With storms that surge in veins untold!

355
00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:55.667
- Hope Raigad is taking good care of you.
- Oh, yes.

356
00:36:57.125 --> 00:36:59.292
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

357
00:36:59.375 --> 00:37:04.125
With storms that surge in veins untold!

358
00:37:10.250 --> 00:37:12.417
O Lord of Lords

359
00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:14.708
O Essence of all

360
00:37:18.958 --> 00:37:21.125
O Mighty One

361
00:37:21.208 --> 00:37:23.333
O Commander of Armies

362
00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:36.042
Come, and take the throne

363
00:37:36.125 --> 00:37:38.208
Come, and claim it as your own

364
00:37:38.292 --> 00:37:40.167
O King Shambhu

365
00:37:40.250 --> 00:37:42.958
Come, the Supreme King

366
00:37:44.708 --> 00:37:49.208
The throne is made for service grand

367
00:37:49.292 --> 00:37:53.167
It is the seat where Gods command

368
00:37:53.250 --> 00:37:56.833
The one that bears responsibility

369
00:37:56.917 --> 00:38:02.833
The one who serves faithfully

370
00:38:04.542 --> 00:38:06.667
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

371
00:38:06.750 --> 00:38:09.375
With storms that surge in veins untold!

372
00:38:12.958 --> 00:38:15.417
The era stirs with a thunderous cry

373
00:38:15.500 --> 00:38:18.125
The storm rises, shaking earth and sky!

374
00:38:19.542 --> 00:38:23.583
In saffron's glory the sky ignites

375
00:38:23.667 --> 00:38:26.833
- Maharaj!
- The storm is here blazing bright!

376
00:38:26.917 --> 00:38:29.792
Puissant and valiant,
the Fort Destroyer,

377
00:38:30.208 --> 00:38:32.875
born of the Kshatriya clan,

378
00:38:33.208 --> 00:38:36.042
the Lord of Thrones,

379
00:38:36.458 --> 00:38:38.792
the King of kings…

380
00:38:39.125 --> 00:38:43.167
Chhatrapati Sambhaji Maharaj!

381
00:38:43.250 --> 00:38:45.667
All praise to thee!

382
00:38:45.875 --> 00:38:49.542
- Hail…
- Goddess Bhavani!

383
00:38:50.375 --> 00:38:52.667
O Ultimate Being

384
00:39:07.458 --> 00:39:09.917
Brave and strong
With sword and spear

385
00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:12.375
A Maratha warrior, with no fear

386
00:39:12.458 --> 00:39:14.917
In battle, your skill is unmatched
Throughout the fight

387
00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:17.375
Sounding the conch
As you claim your right

388
00:39:17.458 --> 00:39:20.083
A ruler of the people

389
00:39:20.167 --> 00:39:22.917
You are like the sun's glow

390
00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:25.542
With Goddess Jagdamba's blessings
Your power will grow

391
00:39:25.625 --> 00:39:28.083
O Chhatrapati O friend Sambha!

392
00:39:28.167 --> 00:39:30.000
- Wonderful!
- Amazing!

393
00:39:31.542 --> 00:39:33.262
A true friend is like the sun
Shining bright

394
00:39:34.250 --> 00:39:36.208
No one compares
To the poet's light

395
00:39:39.833 --> 00:39:40.833
One day…

396
00:39:41.375 --> 00:39:45.583
One day, I shall compete with you
in poetry, Chandogamatya!

397
00:39:45.667 --> 00:39:47.750
In that too,
the victory will be yours, Maharaj!

398
00:39:50.542 --> 00:39:52.292
At times, I cannot understand

399
00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:54.417
whether you are a friend, a servant,

400
00:39:56.333 --> 00:39:58.167
or my shadow, Chandogamatya?

401
00:39:59.125 --> 00:40:00.583
I am like salt, Maharaj.

402
00:40:01.333 --> 00:40:04.042
You may use me whenever
and wherever needed.

403
00:40:04.458 --> 00:40:08.292
Then I shall use you
on my enemy's wounds, Chandogamatya!

404
00:40:09.125 --> 00:40:10.917
It will be my pleasure!

405
00:40:13.333 --> 00:40:16.254
By the grace of Goddess Bhavani,
all transpired with harmony and serenity.

406
00:40:16.792 --> 00:40:19.833
Now, with the Maharaj's permission,
we were thinking of returning to Girkan.

407
00:40:19.917 --> 00:40:22.333
Stay for a few more days, Ganoji.

408
00:40:23.458 --> 00:40:26.417
You are no longer just your sister
and brother-in-law's guest,

409
00:40:27.042 --> 00:40:29.708
you are now the guest
of the Maratha Chhatrapati!

410
00:40:30.625 --> 00:40:32.250
Uncle Hambir, this is his sister's home!

411
00:40:32.750 --> 00:40:35.167
He will feel hesitant to stay here!

412
00:40:41.875 --> 00:40:43.375
I had a request.

413
00:40:43.792 --> 00:40:45.542
On the day of the king's coronation,

414
00:40:46.708 --> 00:40:48.583
you are meant to fulfill Maharaj's wishes.

415
00:40:48.667 --> 00:40:51.000
Yes, not the other way around!

416
00:40:54.000 --> 00:40:56.042
Ganoji and Kanhoji are also my family.

417
00:40:57.917 --> 00:40:59.417
They can ask for whatever they wish.

418
00:40:59.958 --> 00:41:01.000
It's their right!

419
00:41:01.917 --> 00:41:02.917
Please, tell me.

420
00:41:04.250 --> 00:41:08.958
We want the administration of Girkan
to be handed over to us.

421
00:41:13.333 --> 00:41:15.958
If we have the entitlement to our land,

422
00:41:16.042 --> 00:41:19.250
we can make our own decisions
about its development

423
00:41:19.750 --> 00:41:22.833
and we won't need to trouble
you each time, Maharaj!

424
00:41:28.333 --> 00:41:30.250
Ganoji, you should be thinking about

425
00:41:31.333 --> 00:41:33.792
the development of the Deccan,
not just Girkan.

426
00:41:38.292 --> 00:41:39.333
You are right,

427
00:41:40.792 --> 00:41:41.792
but…

428
00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:47.417
Your father promised to give
Girkan's entitlement to my father.

429
00:41:47.542 --> 00:41:49.792
But Abasahib was against
giving entitlement!

430
00:41:50.625 --> 00:41:54.000
In fact, he used to say that
if we start giving special privileges,

431
00:41:54.083 --> 00:41:56.458
people will only think of themselves,

432
00:41:57.083 --> 00:42:01.708
and our own people will destroy our dreams
of Swarajya right before our eyes!

433
00:42:02.167 --> 00:42:05.083
Forget saying that, Abasahib
wouldn't even dream of it, Brother!

434
00:42:05.208 --> 00:42:07.875
This means that either
our father was a liar,

435
00:42:07.958 --> 00:42:09.417
- or your father-in...
- Ganoji!

436
00:42:25.458 --> 00:42:27.917
The Lord of Thrones,

437
00:42:28.208 --> 00:42:30.000
the protector of Swarajya!

438
00:42:30.292 --> 00:42:34.333
Glory to Chhatrapati Sambhaji Maharaj!

439
00:42:40.625 --> 00:42:45.500
This proclamation must have echoed
within your palace, too, Rajmata.

440
00:42:47.042 --> 00:42:48.042
Right?

441
00:42:50.208 --> 00:42:53.125
He has become the Chhatrapati of Swarajya!

442
00:42:55.833 --> 00:42:56.833
Just imagine,

443
00:42:57.875 --> 00:42:59.708
if your own brother,

444
00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.542
Army Chief Hambirrao Mohite,
had stood by you

445
00:43:03.708 --> 00:43:06.292
our vow would have
certainly been fulfilled!

446
00:43:08.542 --> 00:43:09.625
But what now?

447
00:43:12.417 --> 00:43:15.042
Seeing Ramraje as Chhatrapati…

448
00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:17.083
Seems impossible.

449
00:43:19.917 --> 00:43:22.125
Doesn't that sadden you, Rajmata?

450
00:43:54.875 --> 00:43:57.917
Harboring pain only leads
to anxiety, Annaji.

451
00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:01.958
Anxiety breeds restlessness.

452
00:44:03.958 --> 00:44:07.417
Restlessness brings forth worries.

453
00:44:10.083 --> 00:44:12.375
Worries steal away one's sleep,

454
00:44:13.417 --> 00:44:15.750
and with it, all dreams perish!

455
00:44:19.917 --> 00:44:21.792
After Shivaji Maharaj's death,

456
00:44:21.875 --> 00:44:25.500
whenever I sought to capture Shambhu,

457
00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:28.708
Hambirrao stood by him,

458
00:44:29.792 --> 00:44:31.250
and not with me.

459
00:44:33.083 --> 00:44:36.417
So, to turn political dreams into reality,

460
00:44:39.208 --> 00:44:41.542
never expect anything from family!

461
00:44:47.583 --> 00:44:48.917
In such times,

462
00:44:49.875 --> 00:44:51.667
it is strangers who are more useful.

463
00:44:52.042 --> 00:44:53.292
Forgive me, Rajmata,

464
00:44:56.458 --> 00:45:00.000
but when he was just a crown prince,
far from the throne…

465
00:45:03.083 --> 00:45:05.417
All your efforts had failed even then.

466
00:45:08.750 --> 00:45:10.750
Now, he is the Chhatrapati,

467
00:45:13.083 --> 00:45:15.000
the king of the Marathas!

468
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:20.792
Any mistake now,
and disaster will strike.

469
00:45:23.625 --> 00:45:25.708
With the king gone,

470
00:45:27.917 --> 00:45:29.458
who will hold us accountable?

471
00:45:31.000 --> 00:45:32.000
Balaji,

472
00:45:32.500 --> 00:45:35.708
begin writing the final chapter of

473
00:45:35.792 --> 00:45:38.042
Chhatrapati Sambhaji Maharaj's biography!

474
00:46:20.208 --> 00:46:21.792
Chandogamatya,

475
00:46:21.917 --> 00:46:25.208
why does Prince Mirza Akbar
wish to meet me?

476
00:46:26.833 --> 00:46:30.375
Akbar wishes to reveal
the reason only to Maharaj!

477
00:46:32.917 --> 00:46:34.667
All I know is that

478
00:46:35.125 --> 00:46:39.125
Akbar seeks to claim the Mughal crown
while Aurangzeb is still alive!

479
00:46:42.208 --> 00:46:44.208
Aurang's son certainly has fire in him.

480
00:46:46.750 --> 00:46:48.550
There must be an important
reason behind this!

481
00:46:49.792 --> 00:46:53.500
Otherwise, why would he request
to meet the Maharaj in person?

482
00:46:55.042 --> 00:46:58.833
There must surely be a conspiracy
behind his intentions, Maharaj!

483
00:47:00.750 --> 00:47:02.917
Nilopantji is right, Maharaj!

484
00:47:03.958 --> 00:47:07.042
Akbar is, after all, Aurang's blood!

485
00:47:08.708 --> 00:47:09.708
Forgive me, Yesaji,

486
00:47:10.708 --> 00:47:11.917
but until we meet him,

487
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:14.750
we can only guess
about Akbar's true intentions!

488
00:47:15.792 --> 00:47:16.792
I believe…

489
00:47:17.958 --> 00:47:21.458
Any enemy of Aurangzeb
can be useful to us!

490
00:47:22.833 --> 00:47:26.000
If you begin trusting
the Mughals, Kalashji,

491
00:47:26.792 --> 00:47:29.167
we will start losing faith in you!

492
00:47:30.625 --> 00:47:32.125
If he can betray his own father,

493
00:47:33.208 --> 00:47:34.609
how can we expect loyalty from him?

494
00:47:35.583 --> 00:47:37.375
Letting Akbar get close to you

495
00:47:37.708 --> 00:47:39.167
is like playing with fire.

496
00:47:42.917 --> 00:47:44.458
The one who is eager to come

497
00:47:45.708 --> 00:47:48.208
is the very one
I personally sent an invitation to!

498
00:47:53.042 --> 00:47:55.333
Burhanpur is the pillar
of the Mughal Empire!

499
00:47:58.000 --> 00:47:59.375
Though weakened,

500
00:48:00.583 --> 00:48:02.917
Aurangzeb is quickly marching toward us!

501
00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:05.500
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

502
00:48:05.583 --> 00:48:07.292
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

503
00:48:07.417 --> 00:48:09.458
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

504
00:48:09.542 --> 00:48:12.375
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

505
00:48:12.458 --> 00:48:14.458
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

506
00:48:14.542 --> 00:48:16.667
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

507
00:48:16.750 --> 00:48:18.667
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

508
00:48:18.750 --> 00:48:20.792
Chant the name of Lord Rama and Hari!

509
00:48:20.875 --> 00:48:23.083
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

510
00:48:23.167 --> 00:48:25.167
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

511
00:48:25.250 --> 00:48:27.917
Vasudev is here! Vasudev is here!

512
00:48:29.667 --> 00:48:30.792
Tell me, Bahirji.

513
00:48:31.000 --> 00:48:32.208
Greetings, Maharaj!

514
00:48:34.458 --> 00:48:35.819
Did you catch a glimpse of Aurang?

515
00:48:36.958 --> 00:48:38.583
Raje, not just Aurang,

516
00:48:39.875 --> 00:48:41.167
but an army of 800,000,

517
00:48:42.083 --> 00:48:43.333
fifty thousand horses,

518
00:48:44.375 --> 00:48:45.625
thirty thousand elephants,

519
00:48:46.042 --> 00:48:47.375
and treasures in millions.

520
00:48:48.875 --> 00:48:51.208
Perhaps for the first
and last time in history,

521
00:48:51.292 --> 00:48:54.292
a force so mighty has been sent
in search of someone!

522
00:49:02.458 --> 00:49:05.708
Bahirji, stay close to Aurang,
like his shadow.

523
00:49:07.625 --> 00:49:09.625
If he veers off course even slightly,

524
00:49:10.667 --> 00:49:13.125
steer him back towards us
by any means necessary!

525
00:49:15.833 --> 00:49:18.292
In the meantime,
I shall attend to his son!

526
00:50:04.375 --> 00:50:05.375
Shri-Sakhi!

527
00:50:07.750 --> 00:50:11.667
Right from the youngest Maratha soldier
to the army chief, Uncle Hambir himself,

528
00:50:11.750 --> 00:50:12.750
everyone is worried.

529
00:50:13.083 --> 00:50:14.083
Why?

530
00:50:15.250 --> 00:50:18.667
Because I am going to meet
Prince Akbar without my army!

531
00:50:20.625 --> 00:50:23.000
I don't see a trace
of concern in your eyes!

532
00:50:24.042 --> 00:50:25.208
I am worried,

533
00:50:25.667 --> 00:50:26.667
but not for you.

534
00:50:27.708 --> 00:50:28.789
I'm worried for poor Akbar.

535
00:50:31.000 --> 00:50:32.250
On the day of the wedding,

536
00:50:32.375 --> 00:50:34.500
Jija Aausahib told me…

537
00:50:36.167 --> 00:50:38.875
That all men of the Bhonsle family
are like mountain storms.

538
00:50:40.958 --> 00:50:43.167
If even the mountains
cannot withstand their fury,

539
00:50:43.333 --> 00:50:44.833
who else can dare to challenge them?

540
00:50:46.458 --> 00:50:50.333
Sometimes, even storms lose
their strength, Shri-Sakhi.

541
00:50:50.750 --> 00:50:51.750
Maharaj,

542
00:50:52.375 --> 00:50:54.496
please have mercy and refrain
from saying such things.

543
00:50:55.625 --> 00:50:58.208
Someone is eagerly waiting to meet you.

544
00:51:07.167 --> 00:51:08.167
I feel…

545
00:51:08.500 --> 00:51:09.500
It's a boy!

546
00:51:12.417 --> 00:51:14.417
Another mountain storm is coming!

547
00:51:34.167 --> 00:51:35.458
I'll meet him alone.

548
00:51:35.542 --> 00:51:36.542
But Raje…

549
00:52:30.708 --> 00:52:31.833
Glory be to Allah!

550
00:52:31.917 --> 00:52:33.458
Glory be to Allah!

551
00:52:35.333 --> 00:52:37.375
Chhatrapati Sambhaji Maharaj,

552
00:52:37.458 --> 00:52:40.208
you are exactly as I imagined.

553
00:52:42.917 --> 00:52:47.750
While I waited for you
in my tent, sword in hand…

554
00:52:47.833 --> 00:52:49.625
You come here…

555
00:52:50.292 --> 00:52:52.708
Unarmed, to meet me.

556
00:52:54.458 --> 00:52:57.417
I respect my sword.

557
00:52:59.708 --> 00:53:01.292
Moreover, here,

558
00:53:01.667 --> 00:53:03.833
we don't catch a serpent's offspring
with a sword,

559
00:53:04.708 --> 00:53:06.042
we seize it with our fingers

560
00:53:06.875 --> 00:53:09.125
and crush it in our fist!

561
00:53:10.375 --> 00:53:13.750
I simply wanted to see
if the man I sought

562
00:53:14.292 --> 00:53:18.958
would meet me himself
or send an imposter.

563
00:53:19.958 --> 00:53:22.125
Even my imposter
would have swept the floor with them.

564
00:53:23.125 --> 00:53:24.125
Now tell me,

565
00:53:25.292 --> 00:53:27.167
why come as my uninvited guest?

566
00:53:28.000 --> 00:53:31.208
A piece of news has spread
in the North, Maharaj,

567
00:53:31.292 --> 00:53:34.167
that soldiers of the Deccan fear no one!

568
00:53:35.542 --> 00:53:38.542
So I journeyed from my land to yours,

569
00:53:39.083 --> 00:53:43.167
to fulfill my mission with the help
of your brave warriors.

570
00:53:44.333 --> 00:53:45.333
Strange!

571
00:53:46.417 --> 00:53:48.083
Has the North not yet heard

572
00:53:48.167 --> 00:53:51.333
that the warriors of Swarajya
do not fight for the Mughals?

573
00:53:52.625 --> 00:53:53.958
You have taken offense.

574
00:53:55.417 --> 00:53:57.833
I thought you would be easier to convince!

575
00:54:00.167 --> 00:54:01.333
You and I…

576
00:54:02.000 --> 00:54:03.292
Are quite alike.

577
00:54:04.792 --> 00:54:06.750
New generation, new passion,

578
00:54:06.833 --> 00:54:09.458
new ideology, new enthusiasm!

579
00:54:11.208 --> 00:54:14.750
I want every Indian to sit
on the throne of Swarajya…

580
00:54:15.917 --> 00:54:19.375
And you want to kill your father
to take his crown.

581
00:54:19.458 --> 00:54:22.208
There's a vast difference between
my battle and your war, Prince.

582
00:54:23.792 --> 00:54:26.083
That's the nature
of this throne, Raje.

583
00:54:27.667 --> 00:54:30.625
It forces you to spill the blood
of your own kin.

584
00:54:32.167 --> 00:54:34.250
You are only recounting Mughal history.

585
00:54:35.625 --> 00:54:36.917
Look into the Maratha history,

586
00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:39.875
and all you will hear
are stories of bravery!

587
00:54:42.208 --> 00:54:45.000
Do not respect me,

588
00:54:47.125 --> 00:54:49.125
but at least do not insult me, Raje!

589
00:54:51.458 --> 00:54:54.500
Rebellion isn't a trait
of my family alone,

590
00:54:54.583 --> 00:54:56.208
it runs in yours as well!

591
00:55:07.958 --> 00:55:10.292
Welcome to the Deccan, Prince Akbar.

592
00:55:10.875 --> 00:55:12.750
Your enemy is Aurangzeb,

593
00:55:13.375 --> 00:55:15.708
and mine is Sambhaji Bhonsle.

594
00:55:16.208 --> 00:55:20.042
If you aid us in defeating Sambha,

595
00:55:20.333 --> 00:55:25.000
every Maratha will fight beside you
to defeat your enemy.

596
00:55:25.167 --> 00:55:27.292
Once we have both claimed victory,

597
00:55:27.833 --> 00:55:30.667
you may point to any land
on the Deccan map,

598
00:55:31.167 --> 00:55:33.417
and we will give it to you,

599
00:55:33.917 --> 00:55:36.708
beginning a new chapter
in our long-lasting relationship.

600
00:55:36.958 --> 00:55:38.625
Waiting to hear from you.

601
00:55:38.833 --> 00:55:40.167
Rajmata Soyrabai.

602
00:55:51.417 --> 00:55:53.333
I cannot help you,

603
00:55:55.583 --> 00:55:57.208
but I can make this promise…

604
00:55:59.542 --> 00:56:02.042
As long as you stand on Deccan soil,

605
00:56:03.500 --> 00:56:05.458
Aurang can never lay a finger on you.

606
00:56:34.250 --> 00:56:35.250
Maharani!

607
00:56:36.917 --> 00:56:38.417
The beautiful script in which I hoped

608
00:56:38.500 --> 00:56:41.083
to record the successful history
of Swarajya,

609
00:56:41.375 --> 00:56:45.542
you used it to craft a proposal
that would make Maharaj history?

610
00:56:47.042 --> 00:56:48.042
Maharani,

611
00:56:49.708 --> 00:56:51.417
it was indeed written by me,

612
00:56:53.208 --> 00:56:55.958
but the thoughts were not mine.

613
00:56:59.542 --> 00:57:01.125
Forgive me, Maharani!

614
00:57:02.958 --> 00:57:07.083
Just as making mistakes
is a part of being human,

615
00:57:07.458 --> 00:57:10.750
similarly, it is also our duty to forgive.

616
00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:18.000
Forgive me!

617
00:57:18.875 --> 00:57:20.125
Please forgive me, Maharani!

618
00:57:20.708 --> 00:57:21.833
It is not my fault.

619
00:57:21.917 --> 00:57:25.625
I had pardoned your past mistakes

620
00:57:25.708 --> 00:57:28.458
because Swarajya needed your wisdom.

621
00:57:29.375 --> 00:57:33.917
But now,
your greed has outgrown your wisdom.

622
00:57:34.792 --> 00:57:36.250
And your mistakes

623
00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:39.042
have now become a crime!

624
00:57:40.167 --> 00:57:41.917
And to forgive a criminal…

625
00:57:43.542 --> 00:57:46.750
Is itself a crime!

626
00:58:21.208 --> 00:58:22.208
Aaisahib!

627
00:58:23.542 --> 00:58:24.542
Aaisahib!

628
00:58:25.833 --> 00:58:27.125
Aaisahib!

629
00:58:27.792 --> 00:58:28.792
Yes, Shambhu?

630
00:58:29.417 --> 00:58:30.500
Abasahib,

631
00:58:31.000 --> 00:58:33.417
what do these enemies look like?

632
00:58:34.042 --> 00:58:36.083
Why do you ask, Shambhu?

633
00:58:36.917 --> 00:58:39.792
You will never face them.

634
00:58:40.542 --> 00:58:42.667
Your strength is so great

635
00:58:42.958 --> 00:58:45.625
that they will only dare
to attack you from behind.

636
00:58:46.042 --> 00:58:48.875
They will never dare to face you!

637
00:59:05.958 --> 00:59:08.542
I never truly felt a mother's love.

638
00:59:13.917 --> 00:59:17.250
Seeing Soyra Aaisahib's love
for Ramraje,

639
00:59:19.208 --> 00:59:22.958
I realized there are no limits
to a mother's love!

640
00:59:30.542 --> 00:59:32.917
I must have seen my Aaisahib but,

641
00:59:36.292 --> 00:59:38.375
before I could engrave
her face into my memory, she…

642
00:59:47.125 --> 00:59:49.886
I closed my eyes and tried countless times
to find her in my memories.

643
00:59:52.667 --> 00:59:54.833
I even sought her in Soyra Aaisahib.

644
01:00:04.083 --> 01:00:06.167
You know everything,
don't you, Shri-Sakhi?

645
01:00:09.417 --> 01:00:10.417
Please, tell me,

646
01:00:14.625 --> 01:00:17.042
what must my Aaisahib look like?

647
01:00:20.792 --> 01:00:22.583
How could I ever see…

648
01:00:23.667 --> 01:00:26.167
What you cannot, Maharaj?

649
01:00:30.375 --> 01:00:32.833
But I will pray to Goddess Jagdamba

650
01:00:34.375 --> 01:00:37.083
that in the next life,
you are born of my womb.

651
01:00:40.625 --> 01:00:41.625
So that,

652
01:00:42.417 --> 01:00:45.208
I may fulfill both the joys

653
01:00:47.250 --> 01:00:48.542
and shortcomings of this life,

654
01:00:50.125 --> 01:00:52.167
as your mother.

655
01:02:15.208 --> 01:02:17.208
My father, Shah Jahan,

656
01:02:19.667 --> 01:02:20.750
had planned to crown

657
01:02:23.125 --> 01:02:26.542
my brother, Dara Shikoh.

658
01:02:29.000 --> 01:02:30.542
So, I beheaded him.

659
01:02:35.292 --> 01:02:36.583
I adorned his head

660
01:02:38.333 --> 01:02:40.000
and sent it to my father as a gift.

661
01:02:45.250 --> 01:02:46.875
I did not kill Shah Jahan,

662
01:02:49.417 --> 01:02:51.417
I imprisoned him.

663
01:02:55.667 --> 01:02:56.917
For eight years…

664
01:02:59.417 --> 01:03:02.417
For eight long years, he languished,

665
01:03:07.042 --> 01:03:09.583
gazing at the Taj Mahal
through his prison window,

666
01:03:09.667 --> 01:03:11.000
as his life slowly faded away.

667
01:03:15.042 --> 01:03:18.208
Now, a 24-year-old boy…

668
01:03:21.333 --> 01:03:25.000
Has turned my most beautiful city
into a graveyard

669
01:03:26.250 --> 01:03:27.250
and left.

670
01:03:30.708 --> 01:03:31.708
No…

671
01:03:34.250 --> 01:03:35.708
Spare me! Spare me!

672
01:03:38.250 --> 01:03:40.000
How dare you survive?

673
01:04:01.125 --> 01:04:03.417
Sambha has given refuge to Prince Akbar!

674
01:04:12.333 --> 01:04:13.333
Abbahuzur,

675
01:04:15.125 --> 01:04:18.250
Sambha has given refuge to Prince Akbar!

676
01:04:21.583 --> 01:04:26.417
I claimed this crown by stepping
over the dead bodies of my own kin.

677
01:04:55.583 --> 01:04:57.667
Now I will wear it again…

678
01:04:59.542 --> 01:05:02.458
Only when the screams
of that arrogant Sambha…

679
01:05:04.958 --> 01:05:06.833
Ring out across Hindustan!

680
01:05:11.333 --> 01:05:13.750
Wherever you see saffron,

681
01:05:17.250 --> 01:05:18.500
stain it red with blood!

682
01:05:23.500 --> 01:05:26.083
Decorate every fort
in the Deccan with gifts!

683
01:05:27.042 --> 01:05:28.375
Let our guests be welcomed

684
01:05:28.625 --> 01:05:31.250
- with grandeur and festivity!
- We completely agree, Army Chief.

685
01:05:31.542 --> 01:05:34.833
The disagreement we had over
the entitlement last time,

686
01:05:35.208 --> 01:05:38.750
we trust that no doubts remain
about our commitment now!

687
01:05:39.833 --> 01:05:41.250
Doubt is for foes,

688
01:05:41.333 --> 01:05:43.333
for our own,
there is nothing but love, Ganojiraje!

689
01:05:44.208 --> 01:05:46.833
It is said that an uncle
is doubly vigilant than a mother!

690
01:05:48.167 --> 01:05:51.333
And my children are fortunate,
for they have not one, but two uncles!

691
01:05:52.625 --> 01:05:54.417
I trust you will always watch over them.

692
01:05:55.917 --> 01:05:57.167
Don't worry, Maharaj!

693
01:05:58.042 --> 01:06:00.667
We will stand like a shield
against anyone who dares to lay

694
01:06:01.250 --> 01:06:02.833
their evil sights on Swarajya!

695
01:06:22.125 --> 01:06:24.667
I wish Aurang were standing
on that mountain right now!

696
01:06:33.583 --> 01:06:35.208
It feels like a storm is approaching.

697
01:06:35.458 --> 01:06:36.958
Let us go home.

698
01:06:39.875 --> 01:06:41.958
Come on, move, come on.

699
01:06:44.958 --> 01:06:47.083
You can sense it beforehand, right?

700
01:06:47.542 --> 01:06:48.708
Then why didn't you tell me?

701
01:06:49.167 --> 01:06:51.125
Come on, move.

702
01:06:57.083 --> 01:06:58.083
Come on…

703
01:07:16.625 --> 01:07:18.083
Help!

704
01:07:18.208 --> 01:07:19.375
Help me!

705
01:07:19.875 --> 01:07:21.458
Help!

706
01:07:22.000 --> 01:07:23.292
Help!

707
01:07:29.708 --> 01:07:32.917
Raje, almost half of the Mughal army
has reached the Deccan!

708
01:07:34.167 --> 01:07:36.500
My heart trembles
at the sight of their power

709
01:07:36.583 --> 01:07:38.875
and the monstrous cruelty
I have witnessed!

710
01:07:40.292 --> 01:07:42.750
The trees were draped
with more bodies than leaves.

711
01:07:47.833 --> 01:07:49.518
The river ran red with the blood
of our people,

712
01:07:49.542 --> 01:07:50.782
far more than the water itself.

713
01:07:57.833 --> 01:08:00.292
The Mughals have drowned our children,

714
01:08:00.625 --> 01:08:03.417
suffocating the future that once echoed
with laughter and hope!

715
01:08:14.750 --> 01:08:15.750
Get lost!

716
01:08:17.125 --> 01:08:18.875
Mother!

717
01:08:19.875 --> 01:08:21.292
Where do you think you are going?

718
01:08:41.333 --> 01:08:43.167
Wherever Aurang stepped foot,

719
01:08:43.708 --> 01:08:47.167
nothing remained but devastation, Maharaj!

720
01:09:02.708 --> 01:09:04.833
The dust stirred by His Majesty's steps

721
01:09:06.333 --> 01:09:07.917
must have already reached Raigad!

722
01:09:08.250 --> 01:09:09.583
- God willing!
- God willing!

723
01:09:10.167 --> 01:09:12.167
They have only 25,000 soldiers.

724
01:09:13.125 --> 01:09:15.292
And that's just the number of cooks
in our army alone.

725
01:09:17.042 --> 01:09:18.042
Indeed, Zeenat!

726
01:09:18.792 --> 01:09:21.500
And half of our forces
have yet to reach the Deccan.

727
01:09:21.625 --> 01:09:24.708
Now, even God cannot stop my Lord!

728
01:09:31.792 --> 01:09:33.833
Ravage the Deccan
so completely that…

729
01:09:36.375 --> 01:09:40.167
When I see it,
it feels as if it never even existed!

730
01:09:41.417 --> 01:09:43.917
- Let it be so.
- Let it be so.

731
01:09:46.083 --> 01:09:49.042
Until now,
Aurang has advanced like a swift arrow,

732
01:09:50.083 --> 01:09:52.833
but now, he will attempt to surround
us from every side.

733
01:09:53.167 --> 01:09:54.167
His next targets will be

734
01:09:54.792 --> 01:09:55.792
Kalyan,

735
01:09:55.958 --> 01:09:56.958
Bhiwandi,

736
01:09:57.208 --> 01:09:58.208
Jalna,

737
01:09:58.708 --> 01:10:00.542
Nashik, Pune, Satara,

738
01:10:00.958 --> 01:10:01.958
Kolhapur,

739
01:10:02.208 --> 01:10:03.208
Konkan,

740
01:10:04.208 --> 01:10:05.208
and Karnataka!

741
01:10:09.125 --> 01:10:10.542
Raje, we are just 25 thousand,

742
01:10:11.042 --> 01:10:13.500
but our strength
is no less than 25 lakhs!

743
01:10:14.458 --> 01:10:16.098
Just give us the order to charge forward!

744
01:10:20.833 --> 01:10:23.458
We must meet Aurang's
vast army not just with force,

745
01:10:25.042 --> 01:10:26.792
but with strategy, Rayaji!

746
01:10:39.333 --> 01:10:43.208
Just as we bind a wound after
a snake's bite,

747
01:10:44.750 --> 01:10:46.333
the same way, we must…

748
01:10:49.042 --> 01:10:52.042
Secure the entire Deccan
and hold it firmly!

749
01:10:57.500 --> 01:11:01.333
We will attack
in ways they never expect!

750
01:11:01.750 --> 01:11:04.500
The Mughals will not only face our army,

751
01:11:05.042 --> 01:11:07.242
but they will also have to contend
with our land itself.

752
01:11:08.417 --> 01:11:09.417
Indeed, Army Chief,

753
01:11:10.500 --> 01:11:13.500
neither their soldiers
nor their horses are accustomed

754
01:11:13.958 --> 01:11:15.208
to our rugged mountain roads…

755
01:11:16.750 --> 01:11:17.917
And dense forests.

756
01:11:20.500 --> 01:11:22.083
In the dense jungles of the Konkan,

757
01:11:22.917 --> 01:11:25.167
we will strike
like the Monkey Brigade, Maharaj.

758
01:11:26.917 --> 01:11:29.958
We will give them a tour
of our shifting fields.

759
01:11:30.542 --> 01:11:34.250
We will make them taste the sweetness
of Satara's sugarcane.

760
01:11:34.875 --> 01:11:37.435
Raje, we will ensure that the waters
of Nashik turn against them.

761
01:11:38.125 --> 01:11:39.792
We will devour them like crocodiles.

762
01:11:40.625 --> 01:11:44.417
Yes! And in Jalna, we will make
the Mughal army don blood!

763
01:11:45.333 --> 01:11:46.583
We will bury them…

764
01:11:48.250 --> 01:11:50.250
In Kolhapur,
like the fury of an earthquake!

765
01:11:50.958 --> 01:11:52.417
I swear by Goddess Bhavani!

766
01:11:53.708 --> 01:11:55.333
We will reduce Aurang's pride

767
01:11:56.417 --> 01:11:57.500
to ashes!

768
01:11:59.333 --> 01:12:03.042
We must draw them
in like a raging cyclone.

769
01:12:05.208 --> 01:12:07.083
They are here because
we have pulled them here,

770
01:12:08.458 --> 01:12:10.167
and they will leave only
when we decide.

771
01:12:10.542 --> 01:12:11.792
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

772
01:12:11.875 --> 01:12:13.250
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

773
01:12:13.333 --> 01:12:14.542
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

774
01:12:14.625 --> 01:12:16.385
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

775
01:12:52.042 --> 01:12:54.167
I will pray to Goddess Jagdamba…

776
01:12:56.875 --> 01:12:59.167
That all your desires come to fruition!

777
01:14:16.667 --> 01:14:19.125
KONKAN

778
01:15:52.583 --> 01:15:54.417
Send word to every fort commander

779
01:15:55.000 --> 01:15:59.250
to be vigilant of the wandering
Mughal forces nearby.

780
01:16:00.417 --> 01:16:01.833
And Nilopantji,

781
01:16:02.417 --> 01:16:04.208
ensure that in every confrontation,

782
01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:08.500
our army is never short of weapons,
armor, or supplies.

783
01:16:12.208 --> 01:16:14.708
Only the Mughal numbers must dwindle.

784
01:16:17.042 --> 01:16:19.542
SATARA

785
01:16:23.917 --> 01:16:25.125
Don't hurt him!

786
01:16:26.708 --> 01:16:27.833
Spare him!

787
01:16:29.833 --> 01:16:31.042
Do not hurt them!

788
01:16:31.125 --> 01:16:32.125
Spare them!

789
01:18:15.917 --> 01:18:17.833
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

790
01:18:17.917 --> 01:18:20.750
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

791
01:18:21.083 --> 01:18:23.833
Har Har Mahadev!

792
01:18:29.250 --> 01:18:32.667
1681

793
01:19:02.250 --> 01:19:03.250
Uncle Hambir,

794
01:19:05.500 --> 01:19:07.333
if you would permit
your daughter Tara Rani

795
01:19:08.875 --> 01:19:11.958
to marry into the Bhonsle family,
then Ramraje…

796
01:19:23.833 --> 01:19:26.250
JALNA

797
01:21:19.292 --> 01:21:22.792
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

798
01:21:22.875 --> 01:21:26.875
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

799
01:21:26.958 --> 01:21:33.958
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

800
01:22:30.625 --> 01:22:31.458
KOLHAPUR

801
01:22:31.542 --> 01:22:32.542
Let him go!

802
01:22:33.625 --> 01:22:35.167
- Move!
- Let her go!

803
01:22:35.250 --> 01:22:36.667
- Move!
- Let her go!

804
01:22:43.000 --> 01:22:44.167
No…

805
01:22:58.000 --> 01:23:00.167
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

806
01:23:00.250 --> 01:23:02.750
With storms that surge in veins untold!

807
01:23:06.458 --> 01:23:08.917
The era stirs with a thunderous cry

808
01:23:09.000 --> 01:23:11.583
The storm rises, shaking earth and sky!

809
01:23:13.000 --> 01:23:17.167
In saffron's glory the sky ignites

810
01:23:17.625 --> 01:23:20.292
The storm is here blazing bright!

811
01:23:21.958 --> 01:23:26.167
One eye holds tears, the other, desire

812
01:23:26.333 --> 01:23:29.042
The storm has come raging like fire!

813
01:23:30.750 --> 01:23:32.917
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

814
01:23:33.000 --> 01:23:35.625
With storms that surge in veins untold!

815
01:23:39.458 --> 01:23:41.583
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

816
01:23:41.667 --> 01:23:46.417
With storms that surge in veins untold!

817
01:23:52.542 --> 01:23:54.708
O Lord of Lords

818
01:23:54.792 --> 01:23:56.958
O Essence of all

819
01:24:01.292 --> 01:24:03.375
O Lord of Lords

820
01:24:03.458 --> 01:24:05.583
O Essence of all

821
01:24:05.667 --> 01:24:07.750
O Mighty One

822
01:24:07.833 --> 01:24:10.000
O Commander of Armies

823
01:24:10.083 --> 01:24:12.167
He's Narsingh, fierce and bold

824
01:24:12.250 --> 01:24:14.750
With storms that surge in veins untold!

825
01:24:18.500 --> 01:24:20.917
The era stirs with a thunderous cry

826
01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:23.500
The storm rises, shaking earth and sky!

827
01:24:27.583 --> 01:24:29.625
O Mighty One

828
01:24:29.708 --> 01:24:31.875
O Commander of Armies

829
01:24:37.667 --> 01:24:40.917
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

830
01:24:41.000 --> 01:24:43.292
Our army is now only half
of what it once was.

831
01:24:43.667 --> 01:24:45.792
The royal treasury is draining fast.

832
01:24:46.292 --> 01:24:48.167
Find Sambha at once,

833
01:24:48.458 --> 01:24:49.917
or soon enough,

834
01:24:50.000 --> 01:24:53.042
he will turn your beds into graves
and leave without a trace!

835
01:24:53.292 --> 01:24:57.125
It has been many years
since we left Delhi, Your Majesty,

836
01:24:57.417 --> 01:25:00.708
yet not once have we set foot
on a street that Sambha ever crossed.

837
01:25:02.375 --> 01:25:05.417
NASHIK

838
01:25:22.292 --> 01:25:24.042
With a weapon in his grasp

839
01:25:24.125 --> 01:25:27.458
The warrior strikes his foe deep
In the forest

840
01:25:32.167 --> 01:25:34.833
He approaches, his challenge
Echoing through the pack's roar

841
01:25:34.917 --> 01:25:37.417
Swift as the wind

842
01:25:39.000 --> 01:25:41.583
Har Har Mahadev!

843
01:25:42.417 --> 01:25:44.917
He moves in silence beneath the sky

844
01:25:45.000 --> 01:25:47.625
Master of deception

845
01:25:49.333 --> 01:25:50.333
Here he comes

846
01:25:51.708 --> 01:25:52.708
Man of valor!

847
01:25:54.417 --> 01:25:56.917
Mighty Sambhaji!
Man of valor, Sambhaji!

848
01:25:57.000 --> 01:25:58.167
Mighty Sambhaji!

849
01:25:58.250 --> 01:26:00.625
Sambhaji! Chhatrapati Sambhaji!

850
01:26:05.125 --> 01:26:07.583
With a weapon in his grasp

851
01:26:07.667 --> 01:26:10.500
The warrior strikes his foe
Deep in the forest

852
01:26:15.083 --> 01:26:17.750
He approaches, his challenge
Echoing through the pack's roar

853
01:26:17.833 --> 01:26:20.250
Swift as the wind

854
01:26:20.333 --> 01:26:21.500
Sambhaji! Sambhaji!

855
01:26:21.583 --> 01:26:23.375
Chhatrapati Sambhaji!

856
01:28:11.125 --> 01:28:13.083
There is no power or strength
except for Allah!

857
01:28:19.000 --> 01:28:21.667
There is no power or strength
except for Allah.

858
01:28:30.333 --> 01:28:32.125
We have found Prince Mirza Akbar!

859
01:28:33.000 --> 01:28:35.708
If Allah wills, we shall hear good news
before the morning prayer!

860
01:28:36.792 --> 01:28:38.833
Just like Akbar,
there must be someone in the Deccan

861
01:28:40.083 --> 01:28:42.167
who feels trapped in his own house.

862
01:28:46.458 --> 01:28:47.458
Find that person!

863
01:30:08.958 --> 01:30:09.958
Abbahuzur,

864
01:30:10.875 --> 01:30:13.958
the Mughal swords had reached
Akbar's neck, yet,

865
01:30:14.833 --> 01:30:17.875
unfortunately, he's still alive!

866
01:30:21.542 --> 01:30:23.583
But we have found a way
to locate Sambha!

867
01:30:30.583 --> 01:30:32.417
We have found someone
close to Sambha,

868
01:30:32.875 --> 01:30:34.833
who has felt like an outsider
for many years.

869
01:31:05.333 --> 01:31:10.208
Welcome to the Emperor's sanctuary.

870
01:31:13.042 --> 01:31:14.208
Remarkable!
Truly remarkable!

871
01:31:14.542 --> 01:31:15.542
Yashwantji,

872
01:31:16.083 --> 01:31:18.292
the way you and Sampathji

873
01:31:18.375 --> 01:31:20.417
are managing the affairs
of Karnataka and Konkan,

874
01:31:21.083 --> 01:31:23.042
even this poet

875
01:31:23.708 --> 01:31:26.250
cannot find enough words
to praise you today!

876
01:31:28.542 --> 01:31:30.458
What greater fortune
could there be than easing

877
01:31:30.833 --> 01:31:32.250
the burden of Maharaj?

878
01:31:33.125 --> 01:31:34.000
With you there,

879
01:31:34.083 --> 01:31:36.792
I have no need to turn my gaze
in that direction.

880
01:31:37.375 --> 01:31:39.125
Pardon my intrusion, Maharaj,

881
01:31:41.458 --> 01:31:43.250
but the situation is such

882
01:31:43.333 --> 01:31:47.208
that I find myself compelled
to appear before you, uninvited!

883
01:31:49.000 --> 01:31:52.458
I have decided to leave Hindustan.

884
01:32:02.417 --> 01:32:03.417
Prince,

885
01:32:03.750 --> 01:32:05.417
we are so close to achieving our goal.

886
01:32:06.583 --> 01:32:11.667
We did not expect you to leave
at such a critical moment.

887
01:32:11.875 --> 01:32:14.675
I have long harbored this grievance
against the Mughals, Chandogamatya.

888
01:32:16.542 --> 01:32:17.902
They never seek to walk alongside,

889
01:32:19.458 --> 01:32:21.458
they are always fixated on moving forward.

890
01:32:22.625 --> 01:32:26.667
The goal was to march
side by side, Your Majesty.

891
01:32:27.417 --> 01:32:28.417
But right now,

892
01:32:29.792 --> 01:32:33.042
my departure is essential
for me to live a long life.

893
01:32:36.750 --> 01:32:37.750
Why, Prince?

894
01:32:39.125 --> 01:32:41.365
Before the Mughals could lead you
to the gates of heaven,

895
01:32:42.500 --> 01:32:44.625
the Marathas sent them
to the gates of hell.

896
01:32:48.042 --> 01:32:49.333
But for how long, Maharaj?

897
01:32:50.792 --> 01:32:53.417
How long will you be able to protect me?

898
01:32:54.292 --> 01:32:55.625
Your Swarajya

899
01:32:56.042 --> 01:32:58.750
means more to you than my life.

900
01:33:03.542 --> 01:33:07.417
Allow me to say goodbye.

901
01:33:08.625 --> 01:33:09.625
Think it over once more.

902
01:33:11.000 --> 01:33:13.000
You will not be able
to witness Aurang's downfall.

903
01:33:18.458 --> 01:33:20.917
Maharaj, the news of your victory
will bring me immense joy,

904
01:33:21.000 --> 01:33:22.583
even from afar!

905
01:33:23.750 --> 01:33:24.750
Dhanaji!

906
01:33:26.292 --> 01:33:27.292
Yes, Raje?

907
01:33:27.458 --> 01:33:29.667
Ensure that Prince Akbar's plans succeed.

908
01:33:30.792 --> 01:33:31.875
As you command, Maharaj.

909
01:33:31.958 --> 01:33:32.958
Raje!

910
01:33:34.792 --> 01:33:35.792
Raje!

911
01:33:37.250 --> 01:33:38.250
Raje!

912
01:33:39.167 --> 01:33:40.287
What happened, Mhaloji-baba?

913
01:33:41.375 --> 01:33:42.375
Raje,

914
01:33:43.042 --> 01:33:44.583
the army chief is no more.

915
01:33:57.625 --> 01:33:59.833
In the battle of Wai,
while fighting the Mughals,

916
01:34:00.917 --> 01:34:04.042
Army Chief Hambirrao Mohite
breathed his last.

917
01:34:04.250 --> 01:34:06.958
WAI
DECEMBER 1687

918
01:34:07.042 --> 01:34:10.208
The cannon fired
by the defeated Sarja Khan

919
01:34:10.875 --> 01:34:13.958
has breached the walls of Swarajya, Raje.

920
01:34:17.208 --> 01:34:20.542
Accept the final salute

921
01:34:21.625 --> 01:34:27.167
of this soldier of Swarajya, Raje!

922
01:34:28.125 --> 01:34:31.542
Hail Goddess Bhavani.

923
01:34:41.625 --> 01:34:42.792
Goddess Jagdamba!

924
01:35:35.083 --> 01:35:37.750
Shambhu, you must learn to wield a sword

925
01:35:38.083 --> 01:35:39.542
as deftly as your fingers.

926
01:35:40.125 --> 01:35:43.250
Your blade should strike the enemy

927
01:35:43.375 --> 01:35:46.833
with the force of Lord Krishna's
Sudarshan Chakra!

928
01:35:47.208 --> 01:35:48.208
Well done!

929
01:36:01.083 --> 01:36:03.417
Uncle Hambir, please call me Shambhu.

930
01:36:03.833 --> 01:36:05.875
My ears yearn to hear "Shambhu."

931
01:36:07.292 --> 01:36:08.292
Raje…

932
01:36:18.333 --> 01:36:19.333
Yes, Bahirji.

933
01:36:20.083 --> 01:36:21.500
Yashwantji of Karnataka,

934
01:36:22.875 --> 01:36:24.042
Sampathji of Konkan,

935
01:36:25.125 --> 01:36:26.625
Sadanandji of Amravati,

936
01:36:27.958 --> 01:36:29.208
Parshuramji of Goa,

937
01:36:30.958 --> 01:36:32.167
Vinayakji of Kudal…

938
01:36:33.875 --> 01:36:36.792
One by one,
they are falling into Aurang's trap, and

939
01:36:37.500 --> 01:36:39.583
abandoning Swarajya, Raje.

940
01:36:50.250 --> 01:36:51.792
Where is Aurang now?

941
01:36:53.750 --> 01:36:55.917
He has pitched camp in Akluj!

942
01:36:59.000 --> 01:37:01.292
Bahirji, spread the word
among the Mughals,

943
01:37:02.542 --> 01:37:04.667
that 10,000 Maratha soldiers

944
01:37:05.792 --> 01:37:06.958
are marching towards Akluj

945
01:37:08.000 --> 01:37:09.333
via Pune!

946
01:37:10.875 --> 01:37:11.875
Yesaji.

947
01:37:12.167 --> 01:37:13.167
Yes, Raje?

948
01:37:13.583 --> 01:37:16.625
Send a message to every regional chief
in the Deccan to meet me…

949
01:37:18.667 --> 01:37:19.792
In Sangameshwar!

950
01:37:23.542 --> 01:37:24.583
Why Sangameshwar?

951
01:37:25.417 --> 01:37:31.000
Maharaj chose Sangameshwar
to unite all the Marathas.

952
01:37:31.292 --> 01:37:33.000
With a full army,

953
01:37:33.208 --> 01:37:36.083
he will quietly advance through
the dense jungles,

954
01:37:36.250 --> 01:37:37.792
marching towards Aurang.

955
01:37:38.375 --> 01:37:41.583
Meanwhile, the Mughal army spread nearby

956
01:37:41.667 --> 01:37:45.625
will be eagerly waiting
for the 10,000 soldiers in Pune,

957
01:37:45.708 --> 01:37:47.708
who never left Raigad in the first place!

958
01:37:52.542 --> 01:37:53.542
Young Prince?

959
01:37:54.208 --> 01:37:55.208
Bhavani?

960
01:37:55.917 --> 01:37:58.125
Aren't you coming with me
to the temple today?

961
01:37:58.458 --> 01:38:00.875
First, ward off the evil eye
from Maharaj, Dhara.

962
01:38:01.292 --> 01:38:02.583
He is going to war again.

963
01:38:03.917 --> 01:38:05.750
When will this cursed Aurang die?

964
01:38:09.042 --> 01:38:12.208
How many more battles
must you fight, Maharaj?

965
01:38:14.000 --> 01:38:15.417
I hope this is the last one!

966
01:38:21.750 --> 01:38:24.417
I know the pain you all endure
because of it!

967
01:38:28.000 --> 01:38:31.083
To be away from your family for so long,
months turn into years…

968
01:38:36.958 --> 01:38:38.833
Children become unrecognizable!

969
01:38:39.542 --> 01:38:41.502
Maharaj, my brother,
whether you accept it or not,

970
01:38:41.667 --> 01:38:43.417
this time, I too shall join you

971
01:38:43.583 --> 01:38:44.792
in this fight for Swarajya!

972
01:38:48.417 --> 01:38:51.042
You think I am not ready, right?

973
01:38:58.542 --> 01:39:00.000
If I had doubts,

974
01:39:00.083 --> 01:39:03.167
would I have left the entire Raigad
in your care, Ramraje?

975
01:39:06.000 --> 01:39:10.083
Your presence here is more crucial
than my going to battle, Ramraje!

976
01:39:16.167 --> 01:39:17.875
May you live long!

977
01:39:41.583 --> 01:39:42.583
Shri-Sakhi!

978
01:39:43.500 --> 01:39:44.500
Yes?

979
01:39:46.000 --> 01:39:48.042
I am going to face Aurang!

980
01:39:48.125 --> 01:39:50.833
Aren't you worried?

981
01:39:52.250 --> 01:39:53.542
I am,

982
01:39:54.125 --> 01:39:55.125
but not for you.

983
01:39:55.708 --> 01:39:56.708
I am worried for Aurang.

984
01:39:58.208 --> 01:40:00.292
The whole Maratha empire,
including myself,

985
01:40:00.375 --> 01:40:02.375
has been waiting for this day.

986
01:40:03.375 --> 01:40:05.708
To see Aurang's defeat

987
01:40:05.917 --> 01:40:07.833
and the triumph of Abasahib's dreams!

988
01:40:09.000 --> 01:40:10.333
I don't just believe so,

989
01:40:10.833 --> 01:40:11.833
I know so beyond doubt.

990
01:40:16.750 --> 01:40:18.625
With your trust in me

991
01:40:19.125 --> 01:40:20.458
Battles turn to festive displays

992
01:40:23.458 --> 01:40:25.375
Remember, the kingdom's guardian

993
01:40:26.958 --> 01:40:28.917
Must be kept alive always

994
01:40:48.333 --> 01:40:52.833
SANGAMESHWAR

995
01:40:52.917 --> 01:40:56.833
If someone is willing to stoop
to any depth to spread fear,

996
01:40:57.292 --> 01:40:59.125
it is only natural to be afraid of him!

997
01:41:00.292 --> 01:41:04.083
If you have no choice but to follow
the enemy's commands to protect yourself,

998
01:41:05.958 --> 01:41:08.667
I can understand your predicament.

999
01:41:10.667 --> 01:41:12.833
But there is one thing
I cannot comprehend!

1000
01:41:14.500 --> 01:41:17.583
Since when did the Marathas start
thinking only about their own security?

1001
01:41:20.125 --> 01:41:21.125
Yes?

1002
01:41:21.500 --> 01:41:23.208
Every time a Maratha laid down his life,

1003
01:41:23.292 --> 01:41:24.875
it was to protect Swarajya,

1004
01:41:24.958 --> 01:41:27.167
for the glory
of Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj!

1005
01:41:28.833 --> 01:41:32.292
A head that bows only to its motherland…

1006
01:41:32.375 --> 01:41:34.375
How could it ever bow before the enemy?

1007
01:41:38.625 --> 01:41:41.333
Blood of great warriors
runs through our veins!

1008
01:41:41.417 --> 01:41:43.792
Aurang does not possess
the strength to spill it!

1009
01:41:44.875 --> 01:41:46.601
How can a man
capable of killing his father, brother,

1010
01:41:46.625 --> 01:41:48.792
and son for a throne,
ever win our loyalty?

1011
01:41:49.042 --> 01:41:50.583
We are Marathas!

1012
01:41:52.542 --> 01:41:54.018
This throne of Swarajya
has been built through

1013
01:41:54.042 --> 01:41:56.333
the sacrifices and blood
of countless Marathas!

1014
01:41:57.667 --> 01:41:59.458
Swarajya is not the desire of one man,

1015
01:41:59.542 --> 01:42:02.833
it is the will of the Almighty
to protect every soul!

1016
01:42:02.958 --> 01:42:05.958
This kingdom is nothing
but the will of the divine!

1017
01:42:11.708 --> 01:42:12.958
The time has come…

1018
01:42:14.333 --> 01:42:17.000
To rid Hindustan of this monster!

1019
01:42:17.083 --> 01:42:18.083
Now, we make our move!

1020
01:42:21.250 --> 01:42:23.042
Every blow we strike…

1021
01:42:23.750 --> 01:42:26.417
Will honor our fallen martyrs,

1022
01:42:26.500 --> 01:42:28.792
it will be in the name
of Army Chief Hambirrao Mohite!

1023
01:42:30.625 --> 01:42:32.083
I command every regional chief…

1024
01:42:33.167 --> 01:42:34.417
Every Maratha soldier

1025
01:42:35.458 --> 01:42:38.208
of Swarajya must be in Sangameshwar
by tomorrow's sunset.

1026
01:42:39.667 --> 01:42:42.583
In the dead of night, the Maratha army
will advance towards Aurang

1027
01:42:42.750 --> 01:42:44.625
via Amba Ghat, like raging fire!

1028
01:42:46.208 --> 01:42:50.000
We will reduce Aurang
and his hollow empire to ashes!

1029
01:42:50.292 --> 01:42:51.917
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1030
01:42:52.000 --> 01:42:53.375
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1031
01:42:53.458 --> 01:42:54.792
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1032
01:42:54.875 --> 01:42:56.167
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1033
01:42:56.250 --> 01:42:58.708
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!
- Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1034
01:42:58.792 --> 01:43:00.958
Praise be to the consort
of Goddess Parvati!

1035
01:43:01.042 --> 01:43:06.125
- Har Har Mahadev!
- Har Har Mahadev!

1036
01:43:17.083 --> 01:43:18.125
Aaisahib!

1037
01:43:20.125 --> 01:43:21.167
Aaisahib!

1038
01:43:22.167 --> 01:43:23.167
Yes, Shambhu?

1039
01:43:24.125 --> 01:43:25.125
Abasahib,

1040
01:43:25.708 --> 01:43:28.625
when will this tunnel end?

1041
01:43:28.708 --> 01:43:31.208
This tunnel has no end, Shambhu!

1042
01:43:31.667 --> 01:43:33.458
But you shouldn't stop!

1043
01:43:46.583 --> 01:43:49.375
PANHALA FORT

1044
01:43:58.042 --> 01:43:59.208
Oh, wow!

1045
01:44:00.083 --> 01:44:01.333
You seem happy, Father!

1046
01:44:02.875 --> 01:44:04.167
It's not happiness, Santa,

1047
01:44:04.708 --> 01:44:06.458
this is pure excitement!

1048
01:44:07.750 --> 01:44:10.625
Aurang's end is now inevitable!

1049
01:44:12.208 --> 01:44:14.833
Maharaj has already
decided the Mughals' fate.

1050
01:44:15.500 --> 01:44:18.292
Once the order is given, we will strike!

1051
01:44:19.667 --> 01:44:21.958
Did Maharaj forget
to give the orders, Father?

1052
01:44:22.833 --> 01:44:24.083
The army is moving out

1053
01:44:24.417 --> 01:44:25.625
via Amba Ghat.

1054
01:44:44.125 --> 01:44:45.125
What happened, Father?

1055
01:44:45.792 --> 01:44:46.952
We have been betrayed, Santa!

1056
01:44:47.583 --> 01:44:49.542
- It is the Mughal army!
- What?

1057
01:44:49.917 --> 01:44:51.437
They are marching toward Sangameshwar,

1058
01:44:51.583 --> 01:44:52.958
heading straight for Maharaj.

1059
01:44:53.750 --> 01:44:56.708
We must reach Maharaj
before they do, Santa!

1060
01:44:57.000 --> 01:44:58.417
We must hurry!

1061
01:44:58.500 --> 01:45:01.208
- Har Har Mahadev!
- Har Har Mahadev!

1062
01:45:01.292 --> 01:45:02.292
But Father…

1063
01:45:04.458 --> 01:45:07.917
The shortest route to Sangameshwar
is through Amba Ghat!

1064
01:45:10.917 --> 01:45:12.458
How did the Mughals know that?

1065
01:45:34.542 --> 01:45:36.542
We are advancing
with a force of 5,000 men,

1066
01:45:36.875 --> 01:45:39.000
filled with hope.

1067
01:45:39.958 --> 01:45:42.708
If we don't find Sambha
in Sangameshwar, imagine

1068
01:45:44.042 --> 01:45:47.208
what 5,000 frustrated souls
will do to you.

1069
01:46:01.208 --> 01:46:04.833
We too have lived with broken
hearts for years, Muqarrab Khan!

1070
01:46:06.375 --> 01:46:08.250
Why would we do that to anyone else?

1071
01:46:10.208 --> 01:46:11.417
Capturing Sambha

1072
01:46:12.458 --> 01:46:14.167
will fulfill both our dreams!

1073
01:46:15.417 --> 01:46:16.417
Trust me,

1074
01:46:17.042 --> 01:46:18.917
Sambha is in Sangameshwar.

1075
01:46:21.167 --> 01:46:24.833
That too, with just 150 men by his side!

1076
01:46:26.833 --> 01:46:28.583
Glory be to Allah!

1077
01:46:29.542 --> 01:46:30.875
Not just Girkan,

1078
01:46:31.583 --> 01:46:34.292
we shall gift you
the entire Konkan after this!

1079
01:47:12.542 --> 01:47:14.542
Har Har Mahadev!

1080
01:47:15.792 --> 01:47:17.542
Inform Maharaj at once, Santa!

1081
01:47:17.625 --> 01:47:19.333
Har Har Mahadev!

1082
01:47:19.417 --> 01:47:21.667
- Har Har Mahadev!
- Maharaj!

1083
01:47:23.583 --> 01:47:24.726
We are under imminent attack!

1084
01:47:24.750 --> 01:47:26.000
- The Mughals are here!
- Who?

1085
01:47:26.958 --> 01:47:28.000
Kanhoji and Ganoji.

1086
01:47:31.583 --> 01:47:34.375
Charge!

1087
01:47:43.125 --> 01:47:44.125
Raje!

1088
01:47:44.542 --> 01:47:45.542
Raje!

1089
01:47:46.458 --> 01:47:49.917
Who stabbed me in the back
and struck at the heart of Swarajya?

1090
01:47:51.333 --> 01:47:52.583
It was Ganoji and Kanhoji.

1091
01:47:56.458 --> 01:47:58.458
Goddess Jagdamba!

1092
01:48:03.375 --> 01:48:05.500
Depart immediately
to ensure Raigad's safety.

1093
01:48:06.417 --> 01:48:10.167
I am weary of the suspicious
gazes upon me, Maharaj.

1094
01:48:10.458 --> 01:48:13.875
This is my chance to prove my loyalty,
once and for all!

1095
01:48:14.833 --> 01:48:17.958
A faction of 20 warriors stand ready
to escort you safely to Raigad.

1096
01:48:18.125 --> 01:48:21.083
- I beg of you, leave at once!
- Chandogamatya!

1097
01:48:22.167 --> 01:48:24.167
Have you ever seen a chhaava

1098
01:48:24.833 --> 01:48:27.125
fear dogs and run for its life?

1099
01:48:29.333 --> 01:48:31.833
I feel the urge to roar,
like a beast in the jungle!

1100
01:48:32.125 --> 01:48:34.667
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1101
01:51:49.625 --> 01:51:54.000
Anta!

1102
01:51:58.333 --> 01:52:00.292
Anta!

1103
01:52:10.042 --> 01:52:12.583
Raje, accept my final greetings…

1104
01:53:20.167 --> 01:53:21.333
Maharaj!

1105
01:54:17.833 --> 01:54:18.833
Raya!

1106
01:54:28.208 --> 01:54:29.250
Raya!

1107
01:54:34.917 --> 01:54:40.167
Raya!

1108
01:54:45.958 --> 01:54:48.583
Father!

1109
01:55:03.958 --> 01:55:05.542
Father!

1110
01:55:20.875 --> 01:55:23.958
Santaji!

1111
01:55:26.500 --> 01:55:28.643
Leave for Raigad at once
and deliver this to the Maharani!

1112
01:55:28.667 --> 01:55:31.417
No, Maharaj! I cannot leave your side!

1113
01:55:31.542 --> 01:55:32.750
It is my command!

1114
01:55:32.833 --> 01:55:34.375
But what should I tell her?

1115
01:55:35.875 --> 01:55:37.083
She will understand.

1116
01:55:37.167 --> 01:55:38.792
No, Maharaj! No!

1117
01:55:38.875 --> 01:55:39.875
Go!

1118
01:55:40.042 --> 01:55:41.583
Go now!

1119
01:56:11.167 --> 01:56:12.167
This is outrageous!

1120
01:56:12.208 --> 01:56:15.667
Even thousands of soldiers
cannot subdue a single man?

1121
01:56:17.333 --> 01:56:20.042
This king is fiercer
than the king of the jungle!

1122
01:56:27.208 --> 01:56:29.083
As long as his hands remain free,

1123
01:56:30.917 --> 01:56:32.437
nothing will be able to overpower him.

1124
01:58:25.417 --> 01:58:27.792
Raje!

1125
01:58:28.417 --> 01:58:30.167
Raje!

1126
01:58:54.125 --> 01:58:56.375
Raje!

1127
01:59:22.833 --> 01:59:26.333
Raje!

1128
01:59:41.750 --> 01:59:44.667
Take this royal gift to the Emperor!

1129
01:59:56.958 --> 01:59:58.042
Say it again!

1130
01:59:58.958 --> 01:59:59.958
It is true, Emperor.

1131
02:00:00.250 --> 02:00:01.451
Sambha is in Mughal captivity.

1132
02:01:06.500 --> 02:01:07.917
Oh, God,

1133
02:01:10.208 --> 02:01:12.792
your world has been saved
from total annihilation!

1134
02:01:28.833 --> 02:01:30.476
I will go to rescue my brother,
the Maharaj!

1135
02:01:30.500 --> 02:01:31.375
Come with me!

1136
02:01:31.458 --> 02:01:34.250
No matter which path you choose,
the enemy will be waiting to strike!

1137
02:01:34.667 --> 02:01:35.667
Raigad…

1138
02:01:36.750 --> 02:01:39.000
The Mughals have surrounded
Raigad on all sides!

1139
02:01:39.083 --> 02:01:41.583
So, are we to remain here and do nothing?

1140
02:01:43.500 --> 02:01:45.333
Time is of the essence, Crown Prince.

1141
02:01:47.250 --> 02:01:48.875
Swarajya is at risk,

1142
02:01:50.500 --> 02:01:51.500
and Maharaj…

1143
02:01:53.167 --> 02:01:54.958
Is in Aurang's custody.

1144
02:02:07.625 --> 02:02:09.958
Until now, Aurang was far from Maharaj,

1145
02:02:10.167 --> 02:02:12.417
yet our Maharaj made him suffer endlessly.

1146
02:02:13.208 --> 02:02:16.042
Now, Maharaj will face him directly!

1147
02:02:16.375 --> 02:02:17.792
Aurang will beg for death itself!

1148
02:02:19.417 --> 02:02:23.708
Pray that men like Ganoji
and Kanhoji never be born

1149
02:02:23.792 --> 02:02:25.625
even in the enemy's house.

1150
02:04:21.250 --> 02:04:22.250
My Lord…

1151
02:04:32.042 --> 02:04:33.583
Let me…

1152
02:04:35.208 --> 02:04:37.167
Savor this moment, Khan.

1153
02:04:43.708 --> 02:04:44.833
Nine years…

1154
02:04:47.208 --> 02:04:49.875
For nine long years, in every prayer,

1155
02:04:51.292 --> 02:04:53.833
I have pleaded with God
to let me face him.

1156
02:04:57.958 --> 02:04:59.458
Chandogamatya,

1157
02:05:02.042 --> 02:05:05.458
I know this is not the grand court
of Raigad, but still,

1158
02:05:07.083 --> 02:05:10.708
you must do your part
and share a few pearls of wisdom

1159
02:05:10.792 --> 02:05:12.542
to please the Emperor.

1160
02:05:17.167 --> 02:05:21.000
Elephants, horses, cannons, swords

1161
02:05:21.958 --> 02:05:24.667
Your army's strong and vast

1162
02:05:25.958 --> 02:05:29.292
But my King, though chained

1163
02:05:29.583 --> 02:05:32.333
Remains a force to outlast!

1164
02:05:34.042 --> 02:05:36.125
Let us feed his meat to the dogs

1165
02:05:36.750 --> 02:05:38.542
and end his lineage here and now!

1166
02:05:39.875 --> 02:05:40.917
You should feed our meat

1167
02:05:42.417 --> 02:05:44.917
to your dogs only.

1168
02:05:46.167 --> 02:05:49.917
At least your dogs
will get a taste of loyalty

1169
02:05:51.000 --> 02:05:54.792
and their future generations
will be blessed!

1170
02:05:59.333 --> 02:06:00.333
This fails to amuse me.

1171
02:06:08.667 --> 02:06:09.667
Now,

1172
02:06:12.625 --> 02:06:14.167
before I extract…

1173
02:06:16.792 --> 02:06:18.708
Your soul from your body,

1174
02:06:18.792 --> 02:06:20.625
I must ask you one question…

1175
02:06:24.583 --> 02:06:26.208
What is this Swarajya,

1176
02:06:27.875 --> 02:06:30.167
for which you are willing
to give up your life?

1177
02:06:31.375 --> 02:06:32.375
Yes?

1178
02:06:35.917 --> 02:06:38.083
And where is your Swarajya now?

1179
02:06:40.000 --> 02:06:41.833
It is in the mountains of Sahyadri,

1180
02:06:44.083 --> 02:06:46.042
in the flowing waters of the Godavari,

1181
02:06:47.958 --> 02:06:49.917
in the soil of Raigad,

1182
02:06:50.000 --> 02:06:51.667
in the streets of Jalna,

1183
02:06:52.875 --> 02:06:54.417
in the winds of Nashik,

1184
02:06:54.500 --> 02:06:55.833
in every corner of Konkan,

1185
02:06:55.917 --> 02:06:57.542
at the feet of Goddess Bhavani!

1186
02:06:57.625 --> 02:07:00.500
Swarajya dwells in the very veins
of millions of Marathas!

1187
02:07:02.625 --> 02:07:06.542
The Swarajya you wish to destroy,
Aurang, is not just a kingdom.

1188
02:07:08.208 --> 02:07:11.375
It is the vision
of Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj!

1189
02:07:19.792 --> 02:07:21.042
Nothing has changed, has it?

1190
02:07:23.833 --> 02:07:25.708
You stand here,
bound before an Emperor,

1191
02:07:25.792 --> 02:07:27.667
yet your eyes still blaze
with that same fire,

1192
02:07:29.625 --> 02:07:31.375
that same passion ruling your mind.

1193
02:07:34.500 --> 02:07:36.292
Much has changed, Aurang.

1194
02:07:38.667 --> 02:07:40.458
I once saw arrogance in your eyes,

1195
02:07:40.542 --> 02:07:43.375
a crown on your head,

1196
02:07:43.458 --> 02:07:46.125
but both seem to be missing today…

1197
02:07:47.292 --> 02:07:48.750
Emperor!

1198
02:07:57.000 --> 02:07:59.125
Inflict unbearable pain upon him,

1199
02:08:02.208 --> 02:08:05.375
so that when he begs for death,

1200
02:08:08.458 --> 02:08:11.375
all we hear are his screams.

1201
02:08:12.708 --> 02:08:16.250
I dance to the rhythm of death, Aurang!

1202
02:08:16.833 --> 02:08:18.750
You cannot intimidate me with death!

1203
02:08:20.000 --> 02:08:22.583
From my death,
a new Siva and a new Sambha

1204
02:08:22.667 --> 02:08:24.125
will rise in every Maratha home!

1205
02:08:24.250 --> 02:08:25.917
But when you die,

1206
02:08:26.792 --> 02:08:29.500
the Mughal Empire shall fall with you!

1207
02:08:29.583 --> 02:08:31.958
Hail Goddess Bhavani!

1208
02:08:49.250 --> 02:08:51.583
Forgive me, Chandogamatya.

1209
02:08:54.125 --> 02:08:58.292
You have had to endure
this pain because of me.

1210
02:09:00.417 --> 02:09:03.292
In this very pain lies
the joy of life, Maharaj.

1211
02:09:05.667 --> 02:09:07.667
What sorrow can Sudama know

1212
02:09:08.292 --> 02:09:11.417
When compassionate Krishna walks in tow?

1213
02:09:18.625 --> 02:09:20.708
Where are you taking him?

1214
02:09:22.083 --> 02:09:23.500
Are you releasing him?

1215
02:09:28.125 --> 02:09:31.250
His words are like weapons
That change on call

1216
02:09:33.875 --> 02:09:37.292
At times, they become arrows
At times, a sword

1217
02:09:41.500 --> 02:09:42.708
Chandogamatya!

1218
02:09:44.917 --> 02:09:49.042
Do you recall when I said I would

1219
02:09:50.000 --> 02:09:52.458
compete with you in poetry?

1220
02:09:53.625 --> 02:09:55.125
And I responded that

1221
02:09:55.208 --> 02:09:58.000
you are victorious
without a contest.

1222
02:10:01.000 --> 02:10:03.958
The one who masters the mind
Will thrive

1223
02:10:05.208 --> 02:10:07.208
The one who succumbs to it
Won't survive

1224
02:10:08.375 --> 02:10:11.042
Those who yield without a fight

1225
02:10:11.833 --> 02:10:14.292
Bringing upon themselves
Shame every time

1226
02:10:16.000 --> 02:10:19.625
Shame on those
Who fail to dream and strive

1227
02:10:22.292 --> 02:10:27.125
For the right to dream is our birth-right

1228
02:10:28.250 --> 02:10:32.042
For the sake of our own
We must act today

1229
02:10:33.458 --> 02:10:37.500
We must make Swaraj eternal
And immortal, come what may!

1230
02:10:38.375 --> 02:10:40.917
You are a child of the earth

1231
02:10:41.375 --> 02:10:44.625
Not just dust or grain

1232
02:10:45.208 --> 02:10:50.708
You will change the times
And write history

1233
02:10:50.792 --> 02:10:52.042
Do not forget this claim!

1234
02:10:52.333 --> 02:10:55.542
You are the first star of dawn

1235
02:10:56.917 --> 02:10:59.625
The voice of change

1236
02:11:01.833 --> 02:11:04.125
This darkness is fleeting

1237
02:11:04.208 --> 02:11:06.667
Soon the world will be yours to claim!

1238
02:11:10.958 --> 02:11:14.875
Accept your
servant's final greetings, Raje.

1239
02:11:16.000 --> 02:11:17.333
I leave now

1240
02:11:18.083 --> 02:11:21.833
To dwell in the wounds of your foes

1241
02:11:22.708 --> 02:11:24.208
I am salt

1242
02:11:25.167 --> 02:11:27.917
Maharaj, I told you so!

1243
02:11:28.000 --> 02:11:31.250
You are not salt, Poet
You are sandalwood

1244
02:11:32.875 --> 02:11:35.750
You are the pride
I adorn upon my forehead!

1245
02:11:37.792 --> 02:11:40.292
Raje, with that, the contest ends

1246
02:11:41.917 --> 02:11:44.500
In the end
Victory is yours as I had said

1247
02:11:46.542 --> 02:11:51.417
A ruler of the people

1248
02:11:51.750 --> 02:11:56.333
You are like the sun's glow

1249
02:11:56.625 --> 02:12:01.125
With Goddess Jagdamba's blessings
Your power will grow

1250
02:12:01.292 --> 02:12:06.208
O Chhatrapati O friend Sambha!

1251
02:12:07.292 --> 02:12:09.833
I am salt, Maharaj!

1252
02:12:10.167 --> 02:12:12.167
I am salt!

1253
02:12:15.083 --> 02:12:18.583
You are not salt, Poet
You are sandalwood

1254
02:12:20.542 --> 02:12:22.333
You are the pride…

1255
02:12:22.917 --> 02:12:26.250
I adorn upon my forehead

1256
02:12:31.208 --> 02:12:32.708
Raje…

1257
02:12:34.542 --> 02:12:36.958
Tear every nail from his fingers!

1258
02:13:40.167 --> 02:13:41.833
Goddess Jagdamba!

1259
02:13:44.208 --> 02:13:46.125
Goddess Jagdamba!

1260
02:14:04.583 --> 02:14:06.583
We have torn off all the nails,

1261
02:14:07.542 --> 02:14:10.417
yet there is no trace of pain
on Sambha's face.

1262
02:14:40.667 --> 02:14:41.667
Shri-Sakhi!

1263
02:14:41.958 --> 02:14:42.958
Yes?

1264
02:14:44.625 --> 02:14:46.875
Since when did you start
worrying about me?

1265
02:14:48.917 --> 02:14:50.792
Do you question my abilities?

1266
02:14:51.792 --> 02:14:53.792
Or do you doubt my bravery?

1267
02:14:54.042 --> 02:14:58.750
I don't just trust my mountain storm,
I take immense pride in him.

1268
02:15:01.042 --> 02:15:05.125
I might doubt my own existence,
but never your bravery.

1269
02:15:07.250 --> 02:15:11.083
Why do you have such unwavering
faith in me, Shri-Sakhi?

1270
02:15:12.750 --> 02:15:14.333
There must be a reason

1271
02:15:14.958 --> 02:15:16.708
I have yet to understand.

1272
02:15:17.500 --> 02:15:21.333
There is another thing Jija Aausahib
shared with me on the day of our wedding…

1273
02:15:22.083 --> 02:15:25.333
That just as Lord Shiva performed
the tandava on the Himalayas,

1274
02:15:26.000 --> 02:15:30.208
Shambhuraje too will
rule the forts of the Deccan.

1275
02:15:31.000 --> 02:15:35.000
He will illuminate all of Hindustan
with the flame of Swarajya!

1276
02:15:36.958 --> 02:15:37.958
By the way,

1277
02:15:39.000 --> 02:15:42.583
Jija Aausahib also mentioned
something to me…

1278
02:15:43.500 --> 02:15:44.667
She said, "Shambhu",

1279
02:15:45.625 --> 02:15:48.833
Yesu is no ordinary woman.

1280
02:15:49.625 --> 02:15:51.917
She is the very reincarnation
of Goddess Parvati!

1281
02:15:53.667 --> 02:15:57.167
Just as Lord Shiva cannot exist
without Goddess Parvati,

1282
02:15:57.250 --> 02:16:01.000
"similarly, this Shambhu is incomplete
without Yesu!"

1283
02:16:02.042 --> 02:16:05.667
That is why this Sakhi is always
in the heart of her beloved Shri!

1284
02:16:43.917 --> 02:16:45.833
Goddess Jagdamba!

1285
02:16:47.375 --> 02:16:49.375
Goddess Jagdamba!

1286
02:18:02.708 --> 02:18:04.109
He stands there, drenched in blood,

1287
02:18:05.833 --> 02:18:06.958
yet not a single scream,

1288
02:18:08.917 --> 02:18:10.917
not even a whisper
of pain escapes his lips!

1289
02:18:13.917 --> 02:18:16.042
The one who delivers
the blows trembles, my Lord,

1290
02:18:17.667 --> 02:18:20.500
but in Sambha's eyes,
there's not a flicker of fear!

1291
02:18:37.792 --> 02:18:38.792
His eyes!

1292
02:18:59.167 --> 02:19:00.527
What is it that you are gazing at?

1293
02:19:01.542 --> 02:19:02.708
Your eyes.

1294
02:19:03.917 --> 02:19:05.458
And what do you see in them?

1295
02:19:06.625 --> 02:19:08.333
Love, reverence,

1296
02:19:09.000 --> 02:19:11.792
and unwavering pride for Swarajya!

1297
02:19:15.375 --> 02:19:16.583
And for you?

1298
02:19:18.583 --> 02:19:19.958
Only and only love.

1299
02:19:21.042 --> 02:19:25.000
The same love Lord Krishna bore
for Mother Radha in His gaze!

1300
02:19:30.875 --> 02:19:35.708
You know it, and I know too

1301
02:19:36.458 --> 02:19:41.125
I long to live in your love so true

1302
02:19:41.875 --> 02:19:46.833
My eyes are caught in the gaze of you

1303
02:19:47.417 --> 02:19:52.708
I yearn to hold your words, like glue

1304
02:19:52.792 --> 02:19:56.333
You are my world

1305
02:19:56.417 --> 02:19:58.333
At least, close your eyes, Sire.

1306
02:19:58.417 --> 02:20:01.958
-You were, and always will be, eternally
-What are you waiting for? Gouge them out!

1307
02:20:20.625 --> 02:20:22.417
Goddess Jagdamba!

1308
02:20:27.542 --> 02:20:29.708
Goddess Jagdamba!

1309
02:21:35.250 --> 02:21:36.333
Abasahib.

1310
02:21:39.833 --> 02:21:40.917
Yes, Shambhu?

1311
02:21:43.208 --> 02:21:45.667
When I meet Aaisahib,

1312
02:21:46.708 --> 02:21:48.417
how will I know it is her?

1313
02:21:50.667 --> 02:21:53.083
I do not even remember her face!

1314
02:21:55.083 --> 02:21:56.667
But she remembers you, Shambhu.

1315
02:21:57.875 --> 02:22:00.000
Even in the deepest darkness,
if you call her,

1316
02:22:00.083 --> 02:22:03.083
she will recognize you
by your voice alone!

1317
02:22:15.375 --> 02:22:17.292
You cannot intimidate me with death!

1318
02:22:18.500 --> 02:22:21.042
From my death,
a new Siva and a new Sambha

1319
02:22:21.125 --> 02:22:22.667
will rise in every Maratha home!

1320
02:22:22.792 --> 02:22:24.458
But when you die,

1321
02:22:25.333 --> 02:22:28.125
the Mughal Empire shall fall with you!

1322
02:22:31.708 --> 02:22:33.333
Why do such flowers not bloom…

1323
02:22:35.542 --> 02:22:37.292
In our desolate land?

1324
02:23:30.708 --> 02:23:32.000
Align with us.

1325
02:23:34.792 --> 02:23:36.250
Side with the Mughals.

1326
02:23:39.625 --> 02:23:41.105
Your life will change for the better.

1327
02:23:44.375 --> 02:23:46.542
All you have to do
is change your religion!

1328
02:23:58.708 --> 02:24:00.708
Align with us!

1329
02:24:03.500 --> 02:24:05.375
Side with the Marathas.

1330
02:24:07.792 --> 02:24:09.750
Your life will change
for the better and…

1331
02:24:12.500 --> 02:24:14.833
You won't even need
to change your religion!

1332
02:24:25.333 --> 02:24:28.958
Aurang, Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj
is known as the lion,

1333
02:24:30.333 --> 02:24:32.375
and his cub is known as…

1334
02:24:33.625 --> 02:24:37.333
Chhaava!

1335
02:24:53.375 --> 02:24:55.583
Sever his tongue!

1336
02:24:58.708 --> 02:25:00.417
With your trust in me

1337
02:25:01.125 --> 02:25:02.500
Battles turn to festive displays

1338
02:26:08.667 --> 02:26:10.792
Goddess Jagdamba!

1339
02:26:12.417 --> 02:26:14.708
Goddess Jagdamba!

1340
02:26:41.417 --> 02:26:44.000
Puissant and valiant,
the Fort Destroyer,

1341
02:26:44.250 --> 02:26:46.750
born of the Kshatriya clan,

1342
02:26:46.958 --> 02:26:48.833
The King of kings…

1343
02:26:49.208 --> 02:26:53.208
All hail Chhatrapati Ramraje Maharaj!

1344
02:26:57.542 --> 02:26:59.417
With your trust in me

1345
02:26:59.792 --> 02:27:01.250
Battles turn to festive displays

1346
02:27:02.042 --> 02:27:03.958
Remember, the kingdom's guardian

1347
02:27:05.500 --> 02:27:07.250
Must be kept alive always

1348
02:27:08.417 --> 02:27:09.417
Goddess Jagdamba!

1349
02:27:12.292 --> 02:27:15.083
Sambha passed,
rejoicing in his own death,

1350
02:27:15.833 --> 02:27:16.958
while we are left behind…

1351
02:27:18.375 --> 02:27:20.167
To mourn our lives!

1352
02:27:32.333 --> 02:27:34.417
Word has arrived from Raigad.

1353
02:27:41.458 --> 02:27:42.958
The Chhatrapati of the Marathas…

1354
02:27:44.750 --> 02:27:45.917
lives on!

1355
02:27:59.417 --> 02:28:00.417
Mujtaba!

1356
02:28:01.083 --> 02:28:02.083
My Lord.

1357
02:28:12.000 --> 02:28:14.833
If only I had a child like Sambha!

1358
02:28:17.708 --> 02:28:19.250
Just one child, Mujtaba.

1359
02:28:20.500 --> 02:28:22.208
Not only Hindustan,

1360
02:28:22.875 --> 02:28:25.125
but the entire world
would have been mine!

1361
02:28:29.750 --> 02:28:32.125
There burns a fierce envy within me,
for that Siva, Mujtaba,

1362
02:28:35.083 --> 02:28:37.125
who fathered such a chhaava!

1363
02:28:47.667 --> 02:28:48.583
VADHU
11 MARCH 1689

1364
02:28:48.667 --> 02:28:55.667
Your shadow with us…

1365
02:29:00.083 --> 02:29:04.833
Will always thrive!

1366
02:29:04.917 --> 02:29:10.417
May it always thrive

1367
02:29:14.208 --> 02:29:15.292
Aaisahib?

1368
02:29:18.917 --> 02:29:20.083
Yes, Shambhu?

1369
02:29:24.375 --> 02:29:25.893
READY TO SACRIFICE
FOR HIS DUTY TO HIS LAND,

1370
02:29:25.917 --> 02:29:27.292
THE CUB OF SHIVA
MIGHTY AND GRAND.

1371
02:29:27.375 --> 02:29:30.083
A WARRIOR OF VALOR
BOLD AND TRUE,

1372
02:29:30.167 --> 02:29:33.292
NONE OTHER THAN KING SHAMBHU.
